INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_26',
  'Which AWS service helps you centrally manage and govern your AWS environment with multiple accounts, including consolidated billing and organizational units?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations, which provides policy-based management for multiple accounts","AWS IAM Identity Center, for centralized identity management for workforce users","AWS Resource Access Manager, for sharing resources across accounts","AWS Control Tower, which automates the setup of a secure multi-account environment"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Organizations, which allows you to centrally manage and govern your environment with multiple AWS accounts, consolidate billing, and apply policies across accounts. Option B, AWS IAM Identity Center, focuses on identity management. Option C, AWS Resource Access Manager, is for resource sharing. Option D, AWS Control Tower, builds on Organizations to automate landing zone setup. AWS Organizations is the foundational service for multi-account management.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_27',
  'What is the primary benefit of using AWS Control Tower for setting up new AWS accounts?',
  'mcq',
  '["Provides centralized identity management for workforce users across all accounts","Automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment with guardrails and an account factory","Enables sharing of AWS resources like subnets and Transit Gateway attachments across accounts","Offers a centralized dashboard for cost management and detailed reporting across the organization"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes AWS Control Tower''s main benefit: it automates the setup of a well-architected, secure, multi-account AWS environment, including guardrails and an account factory for provisioning new accounts. Option A describes AWS IAM Identity Center. Option C describes AWS Resource Access Manager. Option D describes AWS Cost Explorer and AWS Budgets. These are all incorrect as they do not represent the primary function of AWS Control Tower.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_28',
  'Which service allows you to centrally manage access to multiple AWS accounts and business applications for your workforce users using a single sign-on experience?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), for managing individual user permissions","AWS IAM Identity Center, which provides centralized single sign-on (SSO)","AWS Organizations, for consolidating billing and applying policies across accounts","AWS Resource Access Manager, for sharing resources across accounts"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS IAM Identity Center (formerly AWS SSO), which provides a centralized single sign-on experience for your workforce to access multiple AWS accounts and cloud applications. Option A, AWS IAM, manages permissions within a single account. Option C, AWS Organizations, focuses on account management and billing. Option D, AWS Resource Access Manager, is for resource sharing. Therefore, AWS IAM Identity Center is the correct choice for centralized workforce SSO.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_29',
  'A company wants to enforce mandatory security policies, such as disallowing public S3 buckets, across all newly created AWS accounts within their organization. Which AWS Organizations feature should be used to apply these preventative controls?',
  'mcq',
  '["IAM policies, which define permissions for individual users and roles within an account","Service Control Policies (SCPs), which define the maximum permissions for accounts or OUs","Resource Access Manager (RAM), for sharing resources across accounts","AWS Control Tower guardrails, which are managed rules for compliance"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Service Control Policies (SCPs), which are available in AWS Organizations and allow you to centrally manage permissions for all accounts in your organization. They can be used to set maximum available permissions for accounts, effectively preventing actions like creating public S3 buckets. Option A, IAM policies, are applied within an account. Option C, RAM, is for resource sharing. Option D, AWS Control Tower guardrails, utilize SCPs but SCPs are the direct mechanism for this type of enforcement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_30',
  'What does AWS Organizations primarily help with in terms of governance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Deploying applications to multiple Regions using automated pipelines","Monitoring resource usage and performance metrics for individual services","Consolidating billing and applying policies across multiple AWS accounts","Managing individual user permissions within a single account using fine-grained access controls"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately states that AWS Organizations helps with consolidating billing and applying policies across multiple AWS accounts, which are key aspects of governance in a multi-account environment. Option A relates to CI/CD. Option B relates to Amazon CloudWatch. Option D relates to AWS IAM. These are all incorrect as they do not represent the primary governance function of AWS Organizations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_31',
  'A company needs to provide its employees with single sign-on access to all AWS accounts and integrated third-party business applications. Which service should be implemented for this centralized identity management?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), for managing access within a single account","Amazon Cognito, for managing user identities for web and mobile applications","AWS IAM Identity Center, for centralized access to multiple accounts and applications","AWS Organizations, for managing multiple AWS accounts and consolidated billing"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS IAM Identity Center, which is designed to provide a centralized single sign-on (SSO) experience for your workforce to access multiple AWS accounts and integrated business applications. Option A, AWS IAM, is for managing access within a single account. Option B, Amazon Cognito, is for customer-facing applications. Option D, AWS Organizations, manages accounts but not direct user SSO to applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_32',
  'Which AWS service helps you to create a well-architected multi-account AWS environment with predefined security and compliance guardrails, and an account factory for provisioning new accounts?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations, which manages accounts and consolidated billing","AWS Config, which assesses, audits, and evaluates the configurations of your AWS resources","AWS Control Tower, which automates the setup and governance of a landing zone","AWS Security Hub, which provides a comprehensive view of your security alerts and security posture"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Control Tower, which automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment (a landing zone) with predefined guardrails and an account factory for provisioning new accounts. Option A, AWS Organizations, is the underlying service. Option B, AWS Config, is for configuration management. Option D, AWS Security Hub, aggregates security findings. AWS Control Tower provides the comprehensive solution for this scenario.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_33',
  'What is a key capability of AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM) for multi-account environments?',
  'mcq',
  '["Providing a centralized audit log for all AWS API calls across accounts","Managing user credentials for AWS services and applications","Sharing subnets, Transit Gateway attachments, and other resources across accounts","Automating infrastructure provisioning using templates across multiple accounts"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately identifies a key capability of AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM): it allows you to share various AWS resources, such as subnets, Transit Gateway attachments, and License Manager configurations, across different AWS accounts within your organization. Option A describes AWS CloudTrail. Option B describes AWS IAM or AWS IAM Identity Center. Option D describes AWS CloudFormation or AWS Service Catalog. These are all incorrect as they do not represent the primary function of RAM.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_34',
  'Which AWS service allows you to share specific resources, such as subnets, AWS Transit Gateways, and AWS PrivateLink services, across different AWS accounts within your AWS Organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)","AWS Organizations","AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)","AWS Control Tower"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is the correct service for sharing AWS resources like subnets, Transit Gateways, and PrivateLink services across AWS accounts within an AWS Organization. Option B (AWS Organizations) is used for centralizing billing and governance of multiple AWS accounts, but not for sharing specific resources. Option C (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) provides centralized access management to multiple AWS accounts and business applications, focusing on identity, not resource sharing. Option D (AWS Control Tower) helps set up and govern a secure, multi-account AWS environment but doesn''t directly manage the sharing of individual resources like RAM does.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_35',
  'A company wants to ensure that all new AWS accounts created within its AWS Organization automatically adhere to a baseline set of security and compliance guardrails. Which AWS service provides a prescriptive way to achieve this?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Control Tower","AWS Organizations","AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)","AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Control Tower) is the correct service. It provides a landing zone that automatically sets up a secure, multi-account AWS environment and implements guardrails to ensure compliance and security from the start, automating account vending and governance (anti-pattern: ap-1.2-002). Option B (AWS Organizations) allows for central management of multiple accounts and applying Service Control Policies (SCPs), but Control Tower builds upon Organizations to provide a more prescriptive and automated landing zone. Option C (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) focuses on centralized access management, not environmental governance. Option D (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is for sharing resources between accounts, not for establishing foundational governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_36',
  'A company wants to centralize identity management and provide single sign-on (SSO) access to multiple AWS accounts and business applications for its employees. Which AWS service should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)","AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)","AWS Organizations","AWS Control Tower"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) is the correct service for centralizing identity management and providing single sign-on access to multiple AWS accounts and business applications. It integrates with existing identity sources. Option B (AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)) manages users, groups, roles, and permissions within a single AWS account, but not centralized SSO across multiple accounts. Option C (AWS Organizations) helps manage multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t provide SSO for users. Option D (AWS Control Tower) helps set up and govern a multi-account environment but relies on IAM Identity Center for SSO capabilities.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_37',
  'Which AWS service enables centralized management of multiple AWS accounts, allowing you to consolidate billing, apply Service Control Policies (SCPs), and create Organizational Units (OUs)?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations","AWS Control Tower","AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)","AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Organizations) is the correct service. It allows you to centrally manage and govern multiple AWS accounts, consolidate billing, and apply policies like Service Control Policies (SCPs) across groups of accounts (Organizational Units or OUs). Option B (AWS Control Tower) builds on AWS Organizations to set up and govern a secure multi-account environment, but Organizations is the foundational service for account management. Option C (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) provides centralized access management, not account governance. Option D (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is for sharing resources between accounts, not for overall account management and governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_38',
  'A company wants to ensure that all new AWS accounts provisioned within its organization automatically have a baseline set of security and governance configurations applied. Which AWS service simplifies the setup and management of a multi-account AWS environment with guardrails?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Control Tower","AWS Organizations","AWS Security Hub","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Control Tower) is the correct service. It automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment (landing zone) and provides ongoing governance with guardrails to ensure compliance and security from the start. Option B (AWS Organizations) is the foundational service for managing multiple accounts, but Control Tower adds the automation and prescriptive guidance for a landing zone. Option C (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security alerts and performs compliance checks but does not provision accounts or apply baseline configurations. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance but does not automate the initial setup of a multi-account environment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

