VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_39',
  'A company has a multi-account AWS environment managed by AWS Organizations. They want to ensure that all new accounts provisioned automatically comply with a baseline set of security and governance policies. Which AWS service should be implemented?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Control Tower","AWS Security Hub","AWS Config","AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Control Tower) is the correct service. It provides a managed landing zone that automates the setup of a well-architected, multi-account AWS environment with built-in governance and security guardrails, ensuring new accounts adhere to policies from inception. Option B (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security findings and performs compliance checks but doesn''t provision accounts or apply baseline configurations. Option C (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance but is not an account provisioning and governance service. Option D (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) provides centralized access management, not multi-account governance and provisioning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_40',
  'A company has a multi-account strategy and wants to share specific subnets from a central networking VPC with other application VPCs in different accounts within the same AWS Organization. Which AWS service facilitates this resource sharing?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)","VPC peering connections","AWS Transit Gateway","AWS Organizations"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is the correct service. RAM allows you to share AWS resources, such as subnets, AWS Transit Gateways, and AWS PrivateLink services, with other AWS accounts or within your AWS Organization. This is ideal for sharing centralized networking components. Option B (VPC peering connections) connect two VPCs directly but do not allow sharing of individual subnets. Option C (AWS Transit Gateway) connects VPCs and on-premises networks but RAM is specifically for sharing the underlying resources. Option D (AWS Organizations) manages accounts and applies policies but doesn''t directly manage resource sharing at this granular level.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

