  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)) is the correct service. It provides a centralized place to manage access to multiple AWS accounts and business applications, allowing users to sign in once with their corporate directory credentials to access all assigned resources. Option B (AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)) manages permissions within a single AWS account. Option C (AWS Organizations) manages multiple AWS accounts but does not provide user-level SSO. Option D (AWS Control Tower) helps set up and govern a multi-account environment and integrates with IAM Identity Center for SSO, but IAM Identity Center is the core SSO service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  58,
