  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Organizations) is the correct foundational service. It enables you to centrally manage multiple AWS accounts and apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) to define guardrails and enforce compliance across your organization. Option B (AWS Control Tower) builds upon Organizations to provide a managed landing zone with automated guardrails, but Organizations is the core service for defining and applying these policies across accounts. Option C (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security findings and performs compliance checks but doesn''t enforce policies. Option D (AWS Config) monitors resource configurations for compliance but is not the primary service for enforcing organizational guardrails.',
