  '["AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)","AWS Organizations","AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO)","Amazon Cognito"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS IAM Identity Center (SSO), which provides a centralized way to manage access to multiple AWS accounts and integrated third-party SaaS applications using a single set of credentials, often integrated with an existing corporate directory. Option A manages permissions within a single account. Option B manages multiple AWS accounts but not user access directly. Amazon Cognito (not in scope, but a plausible distractor) is primarily for customer-facing applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

