  '["AWS Organizations account creation API","AWS CloudFormation templates","Account Factory","AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the Account Factory, a core feature of AWS Control Tower that automates the provisioning of new AWS accounts, ensuring they are created with the predefined security, logging, and network configurations (guardrails) of the landing zone. Option A is a programmatic way to create accounts but doesn''t include baseline configuration. Option B could be used but requires manual management of templates and deployment. Option D is for sharing resources, not provisioning accounts.',
