INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_52',
  'Which AWS service allows an organization to centrally manage and govern multiple AWS accounts, enabling consolidated billing, and applying policies across accounts through Organizational Units (OUs)?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations","AWS IAM Identity Center","AWS Resource Access Manager","AWS Control Tower"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Organizations) is the correct answer. It helps you centrally manage and govern your environment as you grow and scale your AWS resources. It provides consolidated billing, allows you to create Organizational Units (OUs) to group accounts, and apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) to those OUs. Option B (AWS IAM Identity Center) provides centralized access management for users. Option C (AWS Resource Access Manager) allows sharing AWS resources across accounts. Option D (AWS Control Tower) builds on AWS Organizations to set up and govern a secure, multi-account AWS environment but AWS Organizations is the foundational service for central management and governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_53',
  'A company is establishing a new multi-account AWS environment and needs to ensure that all new accounts adhere to a predefined security baseline, including mandatory logging, monitoring, and specific security configurations. They want to automate the provisioning of new accounts with these guardrails in place to minimize manual effort and ensure consistency. Which AWS service provides the most efficient way to achieve this?',
  'mcq',
  '["Manually configure each new AWS account using AWS CloudFormation templates.","Deploy AWS Control Tower to set up a landing zone with automated guardrails.","Use AWS Organizations to apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) at the root level.","Develop custom scripts to deploy security tooling and configurations to new accounts."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Deploy AWS Control Tower to set up a landing zone with automated guardrails) is the most efficient and recommended approach. AWS Control Tower automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment (a landing zone) and provides ongoing governance with preventative and detective guardrails, as well as an account factory for provisioning new accounts that conform to the baseline. Option A (Manually configure each new AWS account using AWS CloudFormation templates) and Option D (Develop custom scripts) represent an anti-pattern (ap-1.2-002) of managing centralized security tooling deployment with manual or custom automation, which can lead to inconsistency and higher operational overhead compared to Control Tower. Option C (Use AWS Organizations to apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) at the root level) is a foundational part of governance but SCPs alone don''t automate the deployment of logging, monitoring, or specific configurations; they only set permissions boundaries.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_54',
  'Which AWS service provides a centralized single sign-on (SSO) experience for users to access multiple AWS accounts and cloud applications, simplifying identity management?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)","AWS Organizations","IAM Identity Center (SSO)","AWS Resource Access Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (IAM Identity Center (SSO)) is the correct answer. It enables you to centrally manage SSO access to multiple AWS accounts and applications. Users can sign in once to a user portal and access all their assigned accounts and applications. Option A (AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)) manages permissions within a single AWS account. Option B (AWS Organizations) centrally manages multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t provide the SSO experience for users. Option D (AWS Resource Access Manager) is for sharing resources across accounts.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_55',
  'A development team in an AWS Organization has created a new Amazon VPC subnet and an AWS Transit Gateway attachment in their ''Dev'' account. They need to share these specific network resources with a ''Test'' account within the same organization to allow cross-account connectivity for integration testing. Which AWS service should they use to facilitate this resource sharing securely and efficiently?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)","Amazon VPC peering","AWS Organizations Service Control Policies (SCPs)","AWS IAM Identity Center"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is the correct service. RAM allows you to easily and securely share your AWS resources with any AWS account or within your AWS Organization. It supports sharing various resources, including VPC subnets and Transit Gateway attachments. Option B (Amazon VPC peering) connects two VPCs but is not designed for sharing specific subnets or Transit Gateway attachments across accounts in a managed way. Option C (AWS Organizations Service Control Policies (SCPs)) are used for setting permission boundaries for accounts, not for sharing resources. Option D (AWS IAM Identity Center) is for centralized user access management, not resource sharing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_56',
  'A large enterprise wants to ensure that all new AWS accounts created for various teams automatically comply with a predefined set of security policies, including centralized logging, network configurations, and identity management. They need a solution that automates the provisioning of these accounts with the necessary guardrails. Which AWS service is specifically designed to streamline this process?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Organizations","AWS Control Tower","AWS Service Catalog"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Control Tower) is the correct answer. AWS Control Tower automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment (a landing zone) and provides ongoing governance with preventative and detective guardrails. It includes an account factory for provisioning new accounts that conform to the defined baseline, ensuring automatic compliance. Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is an infrastructure as code service that can deploy resources but doesn''t provide the integrated governance and account factory features of Control Tower. Option B (AWS Organizations) is the foundational service for managing multiple accounts but doesn''t automate the deployment of security baselines or account provisioning. Option D (AWS Service Catalog) allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS, but it''s not designed for initial multi-account environment setup and governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_42_m_42_4_57',
  'An organization wants to delegate the management of specific AWS services, such as Amazon EC2 or Amazon S3, to a dedicated security account within their AWS Organization. This allows the security team to manage these services for all member accounts without granting them full administrative access to the management account. Which AWS Organizations feature enables this capability?',
  'mcq',
  '["Service Control Policies (SCPs)","Organizational Units (OUs)","Delegated administration","AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Delegated administration) is the correct answer. AWS Organizations allows you to delegate administrative permissions for specific AWS services to a member account. This delegated administrator account can then manage the service''s resources and permissions on behalf of the organization without needing access to the management account. Option A (Service Control Policies (SCPs)) are used to set permission boundaries for accounts or OUs. Option B (Organizational Units (OUs)) are used to group accounts for policy application. Option D (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) is for sharing resources, not for delegating administrative roles for services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain42_9',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_42_4',
  'medium'
);

