  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_37',
  'Which AWS service is specifically designed to automate common operational tasks and runbooks, reducing manual effort and potential errors?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS X-Ray","AWS Security Hub"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which allows you to define and execute runbooks to automate routine operational tasks such as patching, instance management, and troubleshooting, significantly reducing manual effort. Option A (incorrect) Amazon CloudWatch is primarily for monitoring and observability, collecting metrics, logs, and events. Option C (incorrect) AWS X-Ray is a service for analyzing and debugging distributed applications, focusing on performance profiling. Option D (incorrect) AWS Security Hub is for aggregating and prioritizing security findings, not for automating operational runbooks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_38',
  'To establish a robust observability strategy for an application, which combination of data types should be collected and correlated to gain comprehensive insights into system behavior?',
  'mcq',
  '["Billing data, usage reports, and cost forecasts","Security findings, compliance reports, and access logs","Metrics, logs, and traces","Instance configurations, network ACLs, and security group rules"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) represents the three pillars of observability: metrics, logs, and traces. Correlating these data types provides a comprehensive view of application and infrastructure behavior, enabling effective troubleshooting and performance analysis. Option A (incorrect) focuses on cost management, which is a different aspect. Option B (incorrect) focuses on security and compliance, which is also a distinct area. Option D (incorrect) relates to infrastructure as code and configuration management, not the real-time operational insights provided by observability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_39',
  'A company aims to achieve higher infrastructure as code maturity by transitioning from manual deployments to fully automated, repeatable processes. Which approach best supports this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implementing manual approval gates for all production changes","Using AWS Management Console for all resource provisioning","Defining infrastructure using CloudFormation or CDK and integrating with CI/CD pipelines","Relying on shell scripts executed directly on EC2 instances for configuration"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) describes the core principle of achieving high infrastructure as code maturity: defining infrastructure using declarative templates (like AWS CloudFormation or AWS CDK) and integrating these definitions into automated CI/CD pipelines. This ensures consistent, repeatable, and auditable deployments. Option A (incorrect) manual approval gates are part of a change management process but don''t contribute to automation or IaC maturity directly. Option B (incorrect) using the AWS Management Console is a manual approach and directly contradicts the goal of automation. Option D (incorrect) relying on shell scripts on instances is an imperative, less mature approach to configuration management compared to declarative IaC, and can lead to drift and inconsistencies.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_40',
  'A Solutions Architect conducted an initial AWS Well-Architected Framework review last year and addressed all identified high-risk issues. To ensure continuous improvement and adapt to new AWS services and best practices, what is the MOST effective strategy?',
  'mcq',
  '["Schedule regular, recurring Well-Architected Reviews, especially after significant architectural changes or production incidents.","Consider the review a one-time compliance exercise, as all high-risk issues have been resolved.","Focus solely on monitoring application metrics and logs, assuming the underlying architecture is optimized.","Delegate future architectural reviews to the development teams without central oversight."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is the most effective strategy. The AWS Well-Architected Framework emphasizes that architecture evolves continuously. Regular reviews, especially after significant changes or incidents, are crucial to surface new improvement opportunities, incorporate new AWS services, and adapt to evolving best practices. This directly addresses the anti-pattern of treating the review as a one-time exercise. Option B (incorrect) represents the anti-pattern [ap-3.1-001], as architecture is not static and continuous improvement is necessary. Option C (incorrect) while monitoring is important, it doesn''t replace the holistic architectural review process. Option D (incorrect) delegating without central oversight can lead to inconsistent application of best practices and missed opportunities for enterprise-wide improvements.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_41',
  'Which capability of AWS Systems Manager Automation allows for the execution of predefined or custom workflows to perform administrative tasks across multiple EC2 instances?',
  'mcq',
  '["Parameter Store for secure configuration management","Run Command for executing commands on instances","Automation documents for defining step-by-step operational procedures","Patch Manager for applying operating system updates"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) refers to Automation documents within AWS Systems Manager Automation, which are JSON or YAML files that define the steps of an operational workflow. These documents enable the execution of complex administrative tasks across multiple instances in an automated and repeatable manner. Option A (incorrect) Parameter Store is for storing configuration data and secrets, not for executing workflows. Option B (incorrect) Run Command is for executing individual commands, which can be a step within an Automation document, but Automation documents themselves define the full workflow. Option D (incorrect) Patch Manager is a specific capability of Systems Manager for patching, not the general mechanism for defining and executing arbitrary operational workflows.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_42',
  'A company needs to improve its operational excellence by gaining deep, correlated insights into its distributed application''s behavior. They are currently collecting metrics with Amazon CloudWatch and logs with CloudWatch Logs. Which additional service should they integrate to trace requests across multiple services and visualize their flow?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS Security Hub","AWS X-Ray","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS X-Ray, which helps developers analyze and debug production, distributed applications, such as those built using microservices. X-Ray provides an end-to-end view of requests as they travel through your application, showing a map of the application''s components, which is crucial for correlating with metrics and logs to gain deep insights. Option A (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager Automation is for automating operational tasks. Option B (incorrect) AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings. Option D (incorrect) AWS IAM Access Analyzer helps identify unintended external access to resources. None of these provide distributed tracing capabilities.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_43',
  'A team is struggling with inconsistent deployments and configuration drift across their environments. They want to move towards fully automated deployments to reduce manual errors and improve operational excellence. Which strategy is MOST effective?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement manual checklists for all deployment steps to ensure consistency.","Use AWS Systems Manager Run Command to manually execute scripts on instances after deployment.","Adopt infrastructure as code (IaC) using AWS CloudFormation or AWS CDK and integrate it with a CI/CD pipeline.","Rely on Amazon EC2 user data scripts to configure instances upon launch, without version control."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the most effective strategy for achieving fully automated and consistent deployments. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with tools like AWS CloudFormation or AWS CDK allows defining infrastructure declaratively, which can then be version-controlled and deployed consistently through automated CI/CD pipelines, significantly reducing manual errors and configuration drift. Option A (incorrect) manual checklists are prone to human error and do not automate the process. Option B (incorrect) using AWS Systems Manager Run Command manually is still a manual step and doesn''t provide the full automation and version control benefits of IaC. Option D (incorrect) relying on EC2 user data without version control or a proper CI/CD integration can lead to inconsistencies and makes changes difficult to track and roll back.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_44',
  'A large enterprise has recently migrated several critical applications to AWS. The operations team is struggling with inconsistent deployment processes, manual incident response procedures, and a lack of standardized monitoring across environments. The Solutions Architect is tasked with establishing a continuous improvement strategy to enhance the overall operational excellence of these applications, specifically focusing on identifying architectural gaps and best practices. The goal is to ensure long-term sustainability and efficiency.

Which approach should the Solutions Architect recommend to systematically identify and address architectural deficiencies and foster a culture of continuous operational improvement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement a comprehensive CI/CD pipeline for all applications using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild, focusing solely on automating deployments to reduce manual errors.","Schedule regular AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews for each critical application, utilizing the AWS Well-Architected Tool to document findings, prioritize risks, and track improvement plans.","Develop detailed operational runbooks for all common incidents and automate their execution using AWS Systems Manager Automation documents, thereby reducing manual intervention during outages.","Centralize all application logs and metrics into Amazon CloudWatch Logs and CloudWatch Metrics, then build custom dashboards and alarms to provide real-time observability."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the most appropriate approach for systematically identifying and addressing architectural deficiencies and fostering continuous operational improvement. The AWS Well-Architected Framework provides a structured methodology to evaluate architectures against best practices across six pillars, including Operational Excellence. Using the AWS Well-Architected Tool helps document findings, prioritize risks, and track improvement plans over time, ensuring a continuous cycle of enhancement. This directly addresses the need to identify architectural gaps and establish a long-term improvement strategy.

Option A (incorrect) focuses on automating deployments, which is a component of operational excellence, but it does not address the broader need to identify architectural gaps across all pillars or establish a continuous improvement framework for the entire operational landscape. It''s a tactical solution, not a strategic framework for assessment.

Option C (incorrect) addresses incident response automation, which is a valuable aspect of operational excellence. However, it is a reactive measure for existing issues rather than a proactive framework for identifying underlying architectural problems and preventing them, which is the primary goal of the Well-Architected Framework.

Option D (incorrect) focuses on observability, which is crucial for monitoring and gaining insights into application health. While essential for operational excellence, it primarily helps in detecting and diagnosing issues rather than systematically identifying and remediating architectural flaws or driving a continuous improvement culture at an architectural level.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_45',
  'A development team wants to ensure their AWS infrastructure deployments are consistent and repeatable. They currently use manual steps for server configuration. Which strategy should a Solutions Architect recommend to improve operational excellence by moving towards a more automated and mature deployment process?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks for all server configuration tasks.","Conduct daily manual checks of server configurations to ensure consistency.","Use the AWS Well-Architected Tool to review infrastructure post-deployment.","Develop custom scripts to be run manually on each server after deployment."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) directly addresses improving operational excellence by automating operational runbooks using AWS Systems Manager Automation. This moves the team from manual steps to an infrastructure as code maturity model, ensuring consistency and repeatability. Option B (incorrect) increases manual overhead and is not a strategy for automation or improving deployment maturity. Option C (incorrect) is a review tool for architecture, not a direct mechanism for automating deployments or server configurations. Option D (incorrect) still relies on manual execution of scripts, which is prone to human error and does not represent a fully automated deployment process, failing to improve operational excellence significantly.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_46',
  'A company wants to establish a proactive operational excellence strategy by ensuring regular architectural reviews and continuous improvement. They are currently treating architectural reviews as a one-time compliance exercise. Which approach should a Solutions Architect recommend to align with AWS best practices?',
  'mcq',
  '["Schedule annual AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews and implement identified improvements.","Focus solely on automating deployment pipelines to reduce manual errors.","Implement AWS Systems Manager Automation for all operational tasks.","Conduct a single, comprehensive review using the AWS Well-Architected Tool and archive the results."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) aligns with the AWS Well-Architected Framework best practice that reviews should be repeated regularly (e.g., annually, or after significant architectural changes or production incidents). This ensures continuous improvement and prevents treating the review as a one-time compliance exercise. Option B (incorrect) is a valid operational excellence improvement but does not address the anti-pattern of one-time architectural reviews. Option C (incorrect) is also an operational excellence improvement but doesn''t address the architectural review process itself. Option D (incorrect) directly embodies the anti-pattern [ap-3.1-001] by treating the Well-Architected Framework review as a one-time exercise, which is not a strategy for continuous improvement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_47',
  'A company''s application frequently experiences performance issues that are difficult to diagnose due to its distributed microservices architecture. A Solutions Architect needs to implement an observability strategy to collect metrics, logs, and traces, and correlate them to gain insights into application behavior and identify bottlenecks. Which combination of AWS services should be recommended?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Security Hub for security findings and Amazon GuardDuty for threat detection.","Amazon CloudWatch for metrics and logs, and AWS X-Ray for distributed tracing.","AWS Systems Manager Automation for operational runbooks and AWS Compute Optimizer for resource recommendations.","AWS IAM Access Analyzer for access policies and Amazon RDS Performance Insights for database tuning."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the ideal combination for an observability strategy. Amazon CloudWatch is used for collecting and monitoring metrics and logs, providing a centralized view of operational data. AWS X-Ray provides end-to-end tracing of requests as they travel through distributed applications, helping to identify performance bottlenecks and service dependencies. Together, they enable comprehensive observability. Option A (incorrect) focuses on security, not observability for application performance. Option C (incorrect) focuses on automation and resource optimization, not on collecting and correlating observability data. Option D (incorrect) focuses on security and database performance, not a holistic observability strategy for a distributed application.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_48',
  'A company is striving for continuous improvement in its operational processes. They want to move beyond basic monitoring and alerting to proactively identify and address operational issues before they impact users. Which aspect of an observability strategy, using AWS services, should a Solutions Architect prioritize to achieve this proactive stance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Focusing solely on collecting basic Amazon CloudWatch metrics for resource utilization.","Implementing comprehensive logging with Amazon CloudWatch Logs and correlating with AWS X-Ray traces.","Conducting monthly AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews for operational excellence.","Automating all operational runbooks using AWS Systems Manager Automation."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) represents a robust observability strategy that moves beyond basic monitoring. Implementing comprehensive logging with Amazon CloudWatch Logs allows for detailed insights into application behavior, and correlating these logs with AWS X-Ray traces provides end-to-end visibility across distributed services, enabling proactive identification of issues and bottlenecks. Option A (incorrect) is a basic monitoring approach and doesn''t provide the depth needed for proactive issue identification. Option C (incorrect) is an important part of operational excellence but is a review process, not a direct observability strategy. Option D (incorrect) is about automation of tasks, which is part of operational excellence, but doesn''t directly enhance the ability to gain insights and correlate data for proactive issue detection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_49',
  'A company is experiencing frequent issues with application deployments due to inconsistent environments and manual configuration steps. A Solutions Architect wants to improve operational excellence by adopting an Infrastructure as Code (IaC) approach and automating the entire deployment pipeline. Which AWS service can be used to manage and automate the execution of configuration changes defined as code?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch for monitoring deployment metrics.","AWS Systems Manager Automation for executing codified operational runbooks.","AWS Well-Architected Tool for reviewing IaC compliance.","AWS X-Ray for tracing deployment process steps."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Systems Manager Automation. While IaC tools like AWS CloudFormation define the infrastructure, Systems Manager Automation can be used to execute codified operational runbooks for post-deployment configuration, patching, and other management tasks, integrating into a fully automated deployment pipeline to ensure consistency and reduce manual errors, thereby improving operational excellence. Option A (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which monitors deployments, but doesn''t execute them. Option C (incorrect) is the AWS Well-Architected Tool, which reviews architecture, not automates deployments. Option D (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which traces application requests, not deployment processes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_50',
  'A Solutions Architect is designing a new application and wants to ensure it adheres to the highest standards of operational excellence. They need a framework to guide their design decisions, focusing on aspects like automation, monitoring, and continuous improvement. Which AWS service provides this structured guidance?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation for automating operational tasks.","Amazon CloudWatch for collecting metrics and logs.","AWS Well-Architected Tool for reviewing against operational excellence best practices.","AWS X-Ray for tracing application requests."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the AWS Well-Architected Tool. It helps you review your architecture against the AWS Well-Architected Framework, which includes the Operational Excellence Pillar. This tool provides structured guidance and best practices for designing and operating workloads, covering automation, monitoring, and continuous improvement, making it ideal for guiding design decisions. Option A (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which is for executing tasks, not for providing architectural guidance. Option B (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which is a monitoring service. Option D (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which is for application tracing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  26,
