  'A Solutions Architect is tasked with migrating an existing containerized application to AWS Graviton processors to achieve better price/performance. Which AWS service can help analyze the current EC2 instances and provide recommendations for Graviton-compatible instance types?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS Security Hub","AWS Compute Optimizer","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Compute Optimizer. It provides recommendations for optimal AWS resources, including identifying opportunities to migrate to Graviton-based EC2 instances for improved price/performance. It analyzes your existing workloads and suggests compatible Graviton instance types. Option A (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager Automation is for automating operational tasks. Option B (incorrect) AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings. Option D (incorrect) AWS IAM Access Analyzer helps identify unintended external access. None of these are designed for Graviton migration analysis and recommendations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_3_42',
  'A large e-commerce application running on Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL is experiencing intermittent performance degradation during peak traffic. The operations team suspects a database bottleneck but lacks clear visibility. Which AWS service combination should a Solutions Architect recommend to identify the specific database performance bottlenecks?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS X-Ray to trace requests and Amazon CloudWatch for basic metrics.","Amazon RDS Performance Insights to analyze database load and query performance.","AWS Compute Optimizer to recommend right-sizing for the RDS instance.","Amazon GuardDuty to detect unusual database access patterns."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon RDS Performance Insights, which provides a visual dashboard to monitor the database load and identify specific SQL queries, users, or hosts that are consuming the most database resources. This is ideal for pinpointing database performance bottlenecks. Option A (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which is excellent for tracing application requests across distributed services, and Amazon CloudWatch provides general metrics, but neither offers deep, specific insights into database query performance like Performance Insights. Option C (incorrect) is AWS Compute Optimizer, which recommends right-sizing, but doesn''t directly identify the root cause of query-level performance bottlenecks. Option D (incorrect) is Amazon GuardDuty, which is a threat detection service, unrelated to performance profiling.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_3_43',
  'A company is migrating a legacy application to AWS and wants to ensure that the new Amazon EC2 instances are optimally sized for both performance and cost. They need a service that can analyze the historical usage of their on-premises servers and provide recommendations for AWS instance types. Which AWS service can assist with this right-sizing effort?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon RDS Performance Insights to analyze database workload.","AWS Compute Optimizer to recommend optimal EC2 instance types.","AWS X-Ray to identify application bottlenecks.","Amazon GuardDuty to detect unusual resource utilization patterns."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Compute Optimizer, which helps you choose optimal AWS resources for your workloads to reduce costs and improve performance by recommending optimal AWS resources based on historical utilization metrics. It can analyze on-premises server data (when integrated with tools like AWS Migration Hub) to provide EC2 recommendations. Option A (incorrect) is Amazon RDS Performance Insights, which is specific to database performance. Option C (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which is for application tracing and bottleneck identification, not for right-sizing infrastructure. Option D (incorrect) is Amazon GuardDuty, which is a threat detection service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_3',
  'medium'
);

