  'A company is considering migrating their on-premises database to Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL. They want to ensure optimal performance and cost-efficiency for the database instance. Which AWS service can provide recommendations for the most suitable RDS instance type and storage configuration based on historical workload data?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon RDS Performance Insights to monitor database load.","AWS X-Ray to trace database queries.","AWS Compute Optimizer to recommend optimal RDS configurations.","Amazon CloudWatch to collect database metrics."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Compute Optimizer, which provides recommendations for optimal AWS resources, including Amazon RDS instances, based on historical utilization metrics. It can help in selecting the most suitable instance type and storage configuration for both performance and cost. Option A (incorrect) is Amazon RDS Performance Insights, which helps in diagnosing performance issues once the database is running, but not in initial right-sizing recommendations. Option B (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which is for application tracing, not for RDS right-sizing. Option D (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which collects metrics, but does not provide automated recommendations for optimal configurations.',
