  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the Reliability pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework. It focuses on ensuring a workload performs its intended function correctly and consistently when it''s expected to, even in the face of infrastructure or service disruptions. This includes topics like recovery planning, fault tolerance, and scaling. Option A (incorrect) Operational Excellence focuses on running and monitoring systems and continuously improving processes. Option B (incorrect) Security focuses on protecting information, systems, and assets. Option D (incorrect) Performance Efficiency focuses on using computing resources efficiently.',
