  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation to automatically remediate reliability issues.","Amazon CloudWatch to monitor resource health and trigger alerts.","AWS Well-Architected Tool to conduct a review against the Reliability Pillar.","AWS Compute Optimizer to recommend more resilient instance types."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the AWS Well-Architected Tool, which allows architects to review their workloads against the AWS Well-Architected Framework, including the Reliability Pillar. This tool provides a structured approach to identify architectural weaknesses, including single points of failure, and offers recommendations for improvement. Option A (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which is used for automating operational tasks and remediation, but not for conducting a comprehensive architectural review. Option B (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which is a monitoring service that can indicate issues but doesn''t provide a framework for architectural assessment. Option D (incorrect) is AWS Compute Optimizer, which focuses on right-sizing for performance and cost, not a holistic reliability assessment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

