  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the AWS Well-Architected Tool, which provides a framework for reviewing workloads against the AWS Well-Architected Framework''s six pillars, including the Reliability Pillar. This tool offers a structured approach to evaluate architectural designs for fault tolerance, disaster recovery, and resilience, identifying areas for improvement. Option A (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which is for automating operational tasks, not for architectural review. Option B (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which monitors operational health, but doesn''t provide a framework for design review. Option D (incorrect) is AWS Compute Optimizer, which focuses on right-sizing, not on comprehensive architectural reliability assessment.',
