  'A security team needs to consolidate security findings from various AWS services like Amazon GuardDuty, AWS IAM Access Analyzer, and AWS Config into a single pane of glass for easier management and prioritization. Which AWS service should a Solutions Architect recommend to achieve this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon CloudWatch to collect and display all security logs.","AWS Security Hub for aggregating and prioritizing security findings.","AWS Systems Manager Automation to run security compliance checks.","AWS X-Ray to trace security-related API calls across services."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Security Hub, which provides a comprehensive view of your security state in AWS and helps you check your compliance with security industry standards and best practices. It aggregates, organizes, and prioritizes security alerts or findings from multiple AWS services (like GuardDuty, IAM Access Analyzer, Config) and partner solutions. Option A (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which is a monitoring service for logs and metrics, but it doesn''t aggregate and prioritize security findings in a dedicated security context like Security Hub. Option C (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which automates operational tasks, including security compliance checks, but it''s not a central aggregation point for findings. Option D (incorrect) is AWS X-Ray, which is used for tracing application requests and identifying performance bottlenecks, not for security finding aggregation.',
