  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS IAM Access Analyzer, which helps you identify the resources in your organization and accounts, such as Amazon S3 buckets or AWS IAM roles, that are shared with an external entity. It continuously monitors and analyzes resource policies to identify unintended external access. Option A (incorrect) is Amazon GuardDuty, which detects threats and malicious activity, but not specifically unintended external access configurations. Option B (incorrect) is AWS Security Hub, which aggregates findings but doesn''t perform the policy analysis itself. Option D (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager Automation, which can automate policy enforcement, but doesn''t analyze existing policies for external access findings.',
