  'The first step is to enable AWS IAM Identity Center (Option A) in your AWS Organizations management account. Next, configure your identity source, which could be the AWS SSO directory, an external Active Directory, or another identity provider (Option C). After the identity source is set up, create permission sets to define the specific access levels users will have in different accounts (Option D). Finally, assign users and groups from your identity source to the relevant AWS accounts and permission sets (Option B).',
