  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is fundamental for collecting and monitoring metrics and logs from all AWS resources and applications. Option B (correct) provides end-to-end visibility by collecting traces, helping to analyze and debug distributed applications. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Automation) is for automating operational tasks. Option D (AWS Compute Optimizer) is for right-sizing resources. Option E (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security findings.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_53',
  'A development team wants to automate routine operational tasks for their Amazon EC2 instances, such as patching, starting/stopping instances, and running custom scripts. They also need to ensure these automations are auditable and repeatable. Which AWS services can help achieve this goal? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation","Amazon CloudWatch Logs","AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Lambda","Amazon EventBridge"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Systems Manager Automation) is specifically designed to automate operational tasks across AWS resources, including EC2 instances, using runbooks. Option B (Amazon CloudWatch Logs) can be used to centralize and monitor logs generated by these automation activities, providing auditable records of execution. Option C (AWS Well-Architected Tool) is for reviewing and improving architecture, not for operational automation. Option D (AWS Lambda) can execute code in response to events but is not the primary service for orchestrating EC2 operational tasks like Systems Manager Automation. Option E (Amazon EventBridge) can trigger automations based on events but doesn''t provide the runbook execution and management capabilities of Systems Manager Automation itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_54',
  'Which AWS services are primarily used for collecting and analyzing observability data, such as metrics, logs, and traces, to improve operational excellence? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS X-Ray","AWS Systems Manager Automation","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS IAM Access Analyzer","AWS Security Hub"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (AWS X-Ray) is a service that helps developers analyze and debug distributed applications, providing end-to-end tracing of requests. Option C (Amazon CloudWatch) is a monitoring and observability service that collects metrics, logs, and events from AWS resources and applications. Option B (AWS Systems Manager Automation) is for automating operational tasks, not primarily for observability data collection. Option D (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) is for identifying unintended external access to resources. Option E (AWS Security Hub) is for aggregating and prioritizing security findings.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_55',
  'A company wants to establish a robust infrastructure as code (IaC) strategy, moving from manual deployments to fully automated, repeatable processes. Which of the following approaches represent key aspects of achieving IaC maturity? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Using AWS CloudFormation to define and provision infrastructure resources.","Manually configuring resources through the AWS Management Console.","Implementing version control for all infrastructure definitions.","Relying on AWS Systems Manager Session Manager for direct server access.","Developing custom scripts for one-time deployments."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Using AWS CloudFormation to define and provision infrastructure resources) is a fundamental practice for Infrastructure as Code, allowing declarative definition of infrastructure. Option C (Implementing version control for all infrastructure definitions) is crucial for IaC maturity, enabling tracking changes, collaboration, and rollback capabilities. Option B (Manually configuring resources through the AWS Management Console) is an anti-pattern to IaC and leads to configuration drift. Option D (Relying on AWS Systems Manager Session Manager for direct server access) is for secure instance access, not for defining or deploying infrastructure as code. Option E (Developing custom scripts for one-time deployments) often lacks the repeatability, idempotency, and version control benefits of a mature IaC solution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
