  '["Amazon CloudWatch","AWS X-Ray","AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS Security Hub","AWS IAM Access Analyzer"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon CloudWatch) is a core monitoring service that collects metrics from virtually all AWS services, providing insights into resource utilization and application performance. Option B (AWS X-Ray) provides distributed tracing, allowing you to visualize and analyze requests as they travel through your microservices architecture, identifying performance bottlenecks. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Automation) is for operational task automation. Option D (AWS Security Hub) aggregates security findings. Option E (AWS IAM Access Analyzer) is for identifying external access to resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_62',
  'A company wants to improve its infrastructure as code maturity by automating deployments and ensuring consistent configurations across environments. Which AWS services and practices are fundamental to achieving this? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Using AWS CloudFormation for declarative infrastructure provisioning.","Implementing version control for all infrastructure templates.","Manually updating resources via the AWS Management Console.","Using AWS Systems Manager Session Manager for direct server access.","Creating custom scripts for one-off configuration changes."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Using AWS CloudFormation for declarative infrastructure provisioning) is a cornerstone of Infrastructure as Code, enabling automated and consistent deployment of resources. Option B (Implementing version control for all infrastructure templates) is crucial for managing changes, collaborating, and maintaining a history of infrastructure definitions. Option C (Manually updating resources via the AWS Management Console) is an anti-pattern to IaC, leading to inconsistencies and configuration drift. Option D (Using AWS Systems Manager Session Manager for direct server access) is for secure remote access, not IaC. Option E (Creating custom scripts for one-off configuration changes) lacks the repeatability and declarative nature of mature IaC practices.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

