INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_71',
  'A large enterprise has a critical financial application running on AWS, which has evolved significantly over the past three years. The development team has been adding features rapidly, but there''s a growing concern about the architecture''s alignment with best practices, particularly regarding operational efficiency and cost. The CTO wants a structured approach to identify architectural risks and improvement opportunities with the LEAST operational overhead for ongoing review and improvement. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Implement a custom script to periodically scan AWS Config rules and generate reports on resource compliance.","Conduct regular AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews using the AWS Well-Architected Tool to identify and track improvements across all pillars.","Engage a third-party consulting firm to perform annual architecture audits and provide recommendations.","Develop an internal checklist based on industry best practices and manually review the architecture quarterly.","Utilize AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews as a continuous process to guide architectural evolution and identify new improvement opportunities."]'::json,
  '{1,4}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option E (correct) correctly identify that conducting regular AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews, facilitated by the AWS Well-Architected Tool, is the most effective and operationally efficient way to identify and track improvements. The Well-Architected Framework provides a structured approach across its six pillars, including Operational Excellence and Cost Optimization, and is designed for continuous application, not a one-time exercise. Option A (incorrect) involves custom scripting which increases operational overhead and may not cover the breadth of the Well-Architected Framework. Option C (incorrect) involves external consultants, which can be costly and may not build internal expertise for continuous improvement. Option D (incorrect) relies on manual processes, which are prone to human error and high operational overhead, failing the constraint.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_72',
  'A global media company operates hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances across multiple AWS accounts. Their operations team frequently performs routine maintenance tasks like patching, stopping/starting instances for cost optimization, and deploying standard configurations. These tasks are currently manual and time-consuming, leading to inconsistencies and potential human errors. The company needs to automate routine operational tasks with high consistency and auditability. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Develop custom shell scripts on a central bastion host to SSH into instances and execute commands.","Utilize AWS Systems Manager Automation to create runbooks for common operational tasks, ensuring consistent execution.","Implement AWS CloudFormation templates to define and deploy instance configurations, then manually apply updates.","Leverage AWS Systems Manager State Manager to maintain desired instance configurations and apply patches automatically.","Use AWS Lambda functions triggered by Amazon CloudWatch Events to execute ad-hoc commands on individual instances."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) involves using AWS Systems Manager Automation to create runbooks, which provides a highly consistent, auditable, and repeatable way to automate operational tasks across many instances and accounts. Option D (correct) uses AWS Systems Manager State Manager to maintain desired configurations and apply patches automatically, which is a key capability for consistent and automated operational excellence. Option A (incorrect) involves manual scripting and SSH, which is insecure, prone to errors, and lacks auditability. Option C (incorrect) uses CloudFormation for initial deployment but suggests manual updates, which defeats the purpose of automation and consistency. Option E (incorrect) uses Lambda for ad-hoc commands, which is less suited for complex, multi-step runbook automation and configuration management compared to Systems Manager.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_73',
  'An e-commerce platform experiences intermittent performance degradation during peak sales events. The operations team struggles to quickly pinpoint the root cause, as they rely on disparate monitoring tools for application metrics, system logs, and request traces. They need a unified approach to correlate data across these sources to accelerate troubleshooting and improve mean time to resolution (MTTR) by enhancing observability. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Consolidate all application logs into Amazon CloudWatch Logs and use CloudWatch Contributor Insights to identify top contributors.","Implement AWS X-Ray to trace requests across microservices and integrate with Amazon CloudWatch for centralized metrics and alarms.","Deploy a third-party APM solution on all EC2 instances to collect metrics and logs, then manually correlate data.","Use Amazon CloudWatch to collect custom metrics from applications and create dashboards, while keeping logs and traces separate.","Utilize AWS X-Ray for distributed tracing and ingest all application and infrastructure logs into Amazon CloudWatch Logs for centralized analysis and correlation."]'::json,
  '{1,4}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option E (correct) both describe effective strategies for enhancing observability by combining AWS X-Ray for distributed tracing with Amazon CloudWatch for centralized metrics and logs. This approach allows for end-to-end visibility of requests, correlation of traces with metrics and logs, and faster root cause analysis, directly addressing the need for improved MTTR. Option A (incorrect) focuses only on logs and Contributor Insights, which is useful but doesn''t provide the full tracing context needed for distributed applications. Option C (incorrect) introduces a third-party solution, which might increase operational overhead and manual correlation efforts, failing the constraint. Option D (incorrect) keeps logs and traces separate, which hinders correlation and makes troubleshooting difficult.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_74',
  'A software development company is migrating its legacy applications to AWS. Currently, infrastructure provisioning is a mix of manual console operations and custom scripts, leading to configuration drift and slow deployments. They aim to achieve a fully automated, repeatable, and version-controlled infrastructure deployment process to ensure higher infrastructure consistency and faster deployment cycles. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Define all infrastructure resources using AWS CloudFormation templates and integrate them into a CI/CD pipeline.","Continue using custom scripts but store them in a version control system like AWS CodeCommit.","Adopt AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks to provision infrastructure components manually.","Implement Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using services like AWS CloudFormation to manage infrastructure definitions.","Use the AWS Management Console for initial setup and then rely on manual configuration for subsequent changes."]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (correct) and Option D (correct) both describe key aspects of achieving infrastructure as code maturity. Defining infrastructure with AWS CloudFormation templates and integrating them into a CI/CD pipeline ensures automation, repeatability, and version control, eliminating configuration drift. Option B (incorrect) improves version control for scripts but still relies on imperative scripting, which is less declarative and harder to manage than IaC. Option C (incorrect) uses Systems Manager Automation, which is great for operational runbooks, but not primarily for defining and provisioning entire infrastructure stacks in a declarative, version-controlled manner. Option E (incorrect) relies on manual console operations, which is the anti-pattern the company is trying to move away from, leading to inconsistency and slow deployments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_75',
  'A large enterprise completed an initial AWS Well-Architected Framework review six months ago, identifying several high-risk items. The team addressed the critical findings but has not revisited the framework since. New services have been adopted, and the application architecture has evolved. The CISO is concerned about potential new risks and missed optimization opportunities. The company needs to ensure continuous alignment with AWS best practices and identify evolving architectural risks. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Treat the initial Well-Architected Review as sufficient for compliance and focus on new feature development.","Schedule regular, recurring AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews, especially after significant architectural changes or production incidents.","Rely solely on automated security scans and performance tests to identify all architectural risks.","Utilize the AWS Well-Architected Tool to document and track the status of identified issues and new design choices over time.","Conduct a comprehensive audit of all AWS resources annually by a third-party firm."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) and Option D (correct) address the anti-pattern of treating the Well-Architected Framework review as a one-time exercise. Regular, recurring reviews, particularly after significant changes, and using the AWS Well-Architected Tool for continuous tracking, are essential for maintaining alignment with best practices and identifying evolving risks. Option A (incorrect) directly embodies the anti-pattern of a one-time review, which is insufficient for evolving architectures. Option C (incorrect) suggests relying solely on automated scans, which are valuable but do not provide the holistic architectural assessment offered by the Well-Architected Framework. Option E (incorrect) is a costly and infrequent approach that doesn''t foster continuous improvement or internal expertise.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_76',
  'A financial institution manages a complex environment with many Amazon EC2 instances that require regular security updates and compliance checks. They want to implement a solution that automatically detects non-compliant instances (e.g., missing patches) and remediates them without manual intervention, while also providing a detailed audit trail. The goal is proactive and automated remediation of security compliance issues with full traceability. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Use AWS Systems Manager Automation to define runbooks that automatically apply patches and configurations based on detected non-compliance.","Manually log into each EC2 instance periodically to check for missing patches and apply them.","Implement AWS Systems Manager State Manager to define desired state configurations and automatically enforce them on instances.","Configure AWS CloudTrail to log all API calls and then manually review logs for compliance violations.","Develop custom scripts to run on a cron job on a central server, which then remotely executes patching commands on EC2 instances."]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) and Option C (correct) both leverage AWS Systems Manager capabilities for automated compliance and remediation. AWS Systems Manager Automation allows defining runbooks for automated patching and configuration, while AWS Systems Manager State Manager ensures instances maintain a desired state, automatically correcting deviations. Both provide audit trails. Option B (incorrect) is a manual process that is inefficient, error-prone, and lacks scalability and auditability. Option D (incorrect) uses CloudTrail for logging, which is crucial for auditability, but it does not provide automated detection or remediation capabilities. Option E (incorrect) relies on custom scripts and remote execution, which is less secure, harder to manage, and lacks the native integration and audit features of AWS Systems Manager.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_77',
  'A development team is struggling with inconsistent environments between development, staging, and production. Manual configuration changes are frequent, leading to ''works on my machine'' issues and prolonged debugging cycles. They want to adopt a strategy that guarantees identical infrastructure configurations across all environments and eliminates configuration drift. (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Standardize on AWS CloudFormation templates to define and provision all infrastructure resources for each environment.","Document all manual configuration steps in a wiki and ensure team members follow them diligently.","Implement AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks to apply configuration changes, but allow manual overrides.","Adopt Infrastructure as Code (IaC) principles to manage all infrastructure definitions in version control.","Use Amazon Machine Images (AMIs) to standardize server builds, but allow manual post-deployment configuration."]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (correct) and Option D (correct) are fundamental to achieving infrastructure consistency and eliminating configuration drift. Standardizing on AWS CloudFormation templates (a form of IaC) and managing all infrastructure definitions in version control ensures that environments are provisioned identically and changes are tracked. Option B (incorrect) relies on manual documentation and human diligence, which is prone to errors and does not prevent drift. Option C (incorrect) uses Systems Manager Automation, which is good for operational tasks, but allowing manual overrides defeats the purpose of consistency and IaC. Option E (incorrect) standardizes the base image but allows manual post-deployment configuration, which reintroduces configuration drift.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_78',
  'A development team wants to ensure their AWS infrastructure deployments are consistent, repeatable, and adhere to best practices for operational excellence. Which AWS services can facilitate the automation of infrastructure provisioning and configuration management? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS CloudFormation","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Well-Architected Tool","Amazon GuardDuty"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Systems Manager Automation) allows for the automation of operational tasks and runbooks, including configuration management and patching, which contributes to operational excellence. AWS CloudFormation (Option B) is an Infrastructure as Code service that enables you to provision and manage AWS and third-party resources, ensuring consistent and repeatable deployments. Amazon CloudWatch (Option C) is primarily for monitoring and observability, not direct infrastructure provisioning. AWS Well-Architected Tool (Option D) helps review architectures against best practices but doesn''t automate deployments. Amazon GuardDuty (Option E) is a threat detection service, unrelated to infrastructure automation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_79',
  'A company wants to move from manual operational procedures to a more automated approach to reduce human error and improve efficiency. Which AWS services can be leveraged to automate routine operational runbooks and enforce desired state configuration? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Automation","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Config","Amazon GuardDuty"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (AWS Systems Manager Automation) allows you to define and execute automated runbooks for common operational tasks, reducing manual effort and errors. AWS Config (Option D) enables you to assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of your AWS resources, helping to enforce desired state configuration and track changes. Amazon CloudWatch (Option B) provides monitoring and alarms, which can trigger automation but is not the automation engine itself. AWS Well-Architected Tool (Option C) is for architectural reviews. Amazon GuardDuty (Option E) is a threat detection service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_80',
  'To ensure an application consistently meets operational excellence standards, a Solutions Architect needs to regularly review the architecture against AWS best practices and identify areas for improvement. Which AWS services are directly involved in facilitating this process? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Systems Manager Automation","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS X-Ray"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (AWS Well-Architected Tool) provides a consistent way to review your architecture against the AWS Well-Architected Framework pillars and offers guidance for improvements. AWS Trusted Advisor (Option D) provides real-time guidance to help you provision your resources following AWS best practices in the areas of cost optimization, performance, security, fault tolerance, and service limits. AWS Systems Manager Automation (Option B) is for automating operational tasks. Amazon CloudWatch (Option C) is for monitoring. AWS X-Ray (Option E) is for application tracing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_81',
  'A company is striving for higher infrastructure as code maturity, aiming to automate deployments and manage configuration changes effectively. Which AWS services can help achieve greater automation and control over infrastructure changes? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Systems Manager Automation","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS IAM Access Analyzer","Amazon RDS Performance Insights"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'AWS CloudFormation (Option A) allows you to define your infrastructure as code, enabling automated, repeatable deployments and updates. AWS Systems Manager Automation (Option B) can be used to automate operational runbooks, including patching, updates, and configuration changes across your instances, which is crucial for managing infrastructure as code maturity. Amazon GuardDuty (Option C) is a threat detection service. AWS IAM Access Analyzer (Option D) helps identify unintended external access. Amazon RDS Performance Insights (Option E) is for database performance monitoring.',
  NOW(),
