  'Option A (AWS Migration Hub) is the correct service. It provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions, offering a consolidated view of your migration portfolio. Option B (AWS Application Discovery Service) is used for collecting data about on-premises servers, but not for tracking migration progress. Option C (AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)) is a rehost migration service, not a central tracking hub. Option D (AWS Database Migration Service (DMS)) is for migrating databases, not for overall migration tracking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_38',
  'A company is evaluating its on-premises applications to determine which ones are suitable for migration to AWS. Which ''R'' of migration involves re-architecting an application to use cloud-native features and services?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost","Replatform","Refactor","Retire"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Refactor) is the correct ''R'' of migration. Refactoring (or re-architecting) involves changing how an application is architected and developed, typically to take full advantage of cloud-native capabilities and improve agility, scalability, and reliability. Option A (Rehost) is lifting and shifting an application without changes. Option B (Replatform) involves making some cloud optimizations without changing the core architecture. Option D (Retire) means decommissioning an application that is no longer needed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_39',
  'A Solutions Architect is advising a company on migrating its legacy monolithic application to AWS. The company wants to minimize initial migration effort and cost, even if it means not immediately leveraging cloud-native benefits. Which migration strategy aligns with this approach?',
  'mcq',
  '["Refactor the application into microservices using AWS Lambda and Amazon DynamoDB.","Replatform the application to run on Amazon ECS with AWS Fargate.","Rehost the application by migrating its virtual machines to Amazon EC2 using AWS Application Migration Service (MGN).","Repurchase a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) solution that replaces the legacy application''s functionality."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Rehost the application by migrating its virtual machines to Amazon EC2 using AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)) is the correct strategy. Rehosting, often called ''lift and shift,'' involves moving applications to the cloud with minimal changes, which directly addresses the goal of minimizing initial migration effort and cost. Option A (Refactor) involves significant architectural changes, increasing initial effort. Option B (Replatform) involves some changes to optimize for cloud, which is more effort than rehosting. Option D (Repurchase) involves replacing the application entirely, which can be a significant undertaking and might not minimize initial migration effort, as it requires re-integration and user training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_40',
  'Which of the 7 Rs of migration involves moving an application to AWS without making any changes to its architecture or code, typically by migrating virtual machines?',
  'mcq',
  '["Replatform","Rehost","Refactor","Relocate"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Rehost) is the correct ''R''. Rehosting, also known as ''lift and shift,'' involves moving an application to the cloud with minimal or no changes to its architecture. Option A (Replatform) involves making some cloud optimizations without changing the core architecture. Option C (Refactor) involves significant architectural changes. Option D (Relocate) is moving hypervisors or entire environments without purchasing new hardware.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_41',
  'A company has identified an on-premises application that is no longer critical to its business operations and has very few users. The Solutions Architect recommends decommissioning this application during the migration planning phase. Which ''R'' of migration does this represent?',
  'mcq',
  '["Retain","Rehost","Retire","Repurchase"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Retire) is the correct ''R''. Retiring an application means decommissioning it because it''s no longer needed or its functionality can be replaced by other means, thus saving resources. Option A (Retain) means keeping the application in the current environment. Option B (Rehost) means moving it to the cloud as-is. Option D (Repurchase) means replacing it with a new SaaS solution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_42',
  'A large enterprise is planning to migrate hundreds of on-premises applications to AWS. The migration team has identified several legacy applications that are critical for business operations but are tightly coupled, have significant technical debt, and require extensive re-engineering to run efficiently in a cloud-native environment. The business stakeholders, however, are pushing for a rapid migration to meet an aggressive timeline, prioritizing minimal initial disruption over long-term optimization. The Solutions Architect must recommend a strategy for these specific applications that balances the business''s need for speed with the technical challenges, while still setting the stage for future modernization.',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost the applications to Amazon EC2 instances using AWS Application Migration Service (MGN), then plan for a future refactoring phase.","Refactor the applications into microservices on Amazon ECS or AWS Lambda before migration to fully leverage cloud-native benefits immediately.","Repurchase commercial off-the-shelf (COTS) alternatives in AWS Marketplace to replace the legacy applications entirely, minimizing custom development.","Retire the legacy applications and rebuild them from scratch using modern serverless architectures to ensure optimal performance and scalability from day one."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) recommends rehosting the applications using AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) and then planning for a future refactoring phase. This approach aligns with the ''rehost'' (lift and shift) strategy, which allows for rapid migration with minimal initial disruption, meeting the aggressive timeline. It acknowledges the technical debt but defers the complex modernization effort, making it a practical first step for legacy applications under time pressure, while still allowing for future refactoring to achieve cloud-native benefits. Option B (incorrect) suggests refactoring immediately. While refactoring is a desirable long-term goal, attempting it before migration for tightly coupled legacy applications with significant technical debt would contradict the business''s aggressive timeline and prioritize extensive re-engineering over rapid migration. This represents a common anti-pattern of over-optimizing too early. Option C (incorrect) proposes repurchasing COTS alternatives. This might be viable for some applications but is unlikely for ''critical, tightly coupled, custom legacy applications'' that are described as needing re-engineering, implying unique business logic not easily replaced by off-the-shelf solutions. Option D (incorrect) suggests retiring and rebuilding from scratch. This is a ''re-architect'' or ''refactor'' strategy, which, similar to Option B, would involve significant upfront development effort and time, directly conflicting with the business''s need for a rapid migration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_43',
  'Which AWS service provides a centralized hub to track the progress of application migrations from on-premises environments to AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS Migration Hub","AWS Control Tower","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Migration Hub) is the correct service. It provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions. Option A (AWS Application Discovery Service) is used to discover on-premises applications and collect data, which feeds into Migration Hub, but it''s not the tracking hub itself. Option C (AWS Control Tower) helps set up and govern a secure, multi-account AWS environment. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) helps you manage your AWS resources and on-premises servers, but it''s not specifically designed for migration tracking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_44',
  'Which of the 7 Rs of migration involves moving an application to a new platform, such as migrating a monolithic application to a containerized environment on Amazon ECS?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rehost","Retire","Replatform","Refactor"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Replatform) is the correct answer. Replatforming (also known as ''lift-and-reshape'') involves making some cloud-native optimizations to realize benefits without changing the core architecture of the application. Migrating to a containerized environment like Amazon ECS while keeping the application logic largely intact is an example of replatforming. Option A (Rehost) is ''lift-and-shift'' with no changes. Option B (Retire) means decommissioning applications that are no longer needed. Option D (Refactor) involves completely re-architecting the application, often to a serverless or microservices pattern, to fully leverage cloud-native features.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_45',
