  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_49',
  'A Solutions Architect is conducting a Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) analysis for migrating an on-premises data center to AWS. Which aspect is a key consideration when calculating the TCO for cloud migration?',
  'mcq',
  '["The number of physical servers in the current data center.","The exact number of CPU cores and RAM in each on-premises server.","The ongoing operational costs, including power, cooling, and maintenance, in addition to compute and storage costs.","The specific brand and model of networking equipment used on-premises."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (The ongoing operational costs, including power, cooling, and maintenance, in addition to compute and storage costs) is the correct answer. TCO analysis for cloud migration involves comparing the total cost of running workloads on-premises versus in the cloud, encompassing not just direct infrastructure costs (compute, storage) but also indirect costs like data center facilities (power, cooling, space), IT labor, software licenses, and maintenance. Options A, B, and D are specific details of the on-premises environment that contribute to the TCO calculation but are not the overarching key consideration of ''ongoing operational costs'' that TCO aims to capture comprehensively.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_50',
  'A company has identified an on-premises application that is critical but cannot be easily re-architected or replatformed due to its complexity and tight coupling with existing infrastructure. They decide to move it to AWS with minimal changes. Which of the 7 Rs of migration applies to this strategy?',
  'mcq',
  '["Refactor","Repurchase","Rehost","Retain"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Rehost) is the correct answer. Rehosting, also known as ''lift-and-shift,'' involves moving an application to AWS without making significant changes to its architecture. This strategy is often chosen for complex legacy applications where the effort of re-architecting is too high or not immediately feasible. Option A (Refactor) involves significant re-architecting. Option B (Repurchase) means moving to a new SaaS solution. Option D (Retain) means keeping the application on-premises.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_51',
  'A Solutions Architect is planning a migration of several on-premises applications to AWS. They need a service to automatically discover application components, visualize dependencies, and collect usage data to inform migration strategies. Which AWS service provides these capabilities?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Migration Hub","AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS Control Tower","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Application Discovery Service) is the correct choice. This service helps you discover on-premises application components, collect detailed information about their configuration, usage, and performance, and visualize dependencies, which is crucial for effective migration planning. Option A (AWS Migration Hub) provides a centralized dashboard to track migration progress but relies on discovery tools like Application Discovery Service. Option C (AWS Control Tower) is for multi-account governance. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational management, not specifically for pre-migration discovery and dependency mapping.',
  NOW(),
