INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_41',
  'Which AWS storage service provides network file system (NFS) access for multiple Amazon EC2 instances, allowing them to share a common, scalable file system?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EBS","Amazon S3","Amazon EFS","Amazon DynamoDB"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon EFS) is the correct service. Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) provides a simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources, accessible via NFS protocol. Option A (Amazon EBS) provides block storage for a single EC2 instance. Option B (Amazon S3) is object storage. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_42',
  'A company needs a managed service for deploying, managing, and scaling containerized applications using the Kubernetes orchestration system. Which AWS service fulfills this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon ECS","Amazon EKS","AWS Lambda","Amazon EC2"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon EKS) is the correct service. Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) is a managed service that makes it easy to run Kubernetes on AWS without needing to install, operate, and maintain your own Kubernetes control plane. Option A (Amazon ECS) is another container orchestration service but uses its own orchestrator, not Kubernetes. Option C (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service for functions. Option D (Amazon EC2) provides virtual servers, but not managed Kubernetes orchestration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_43',
  'Which AWS service provides high-performance, fully managed file storage for compute-intensive workloads, with options for both Lustre and Windows File Server file systems?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EFS","Amazon S3","Amazon EBS","Amazon FSx"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (Amazon FSx) is the correct service. Amazon FSx provides fully managed third-party file systems with native compatibility and feature sets for specific workloads, including Amazon FSx for Lustre (for high-performance computing) and Amazon FSx for Windows File Server. Option A (Amazon EFS) is a general-purpose NFS file system. Option B (Amazon S3) is object storage. Option C (Amazon EBS) is block storage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_44',
  'A Solutions Architect is designing a new application that requires a search and analytics engine for operational logs and application metrics. Which AWS service is best suited for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon RDS","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon OpenSearch Service","Amazon SQS"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon OpenSearch Service) is the correct service. Amazon OpenSearch Service (formerly Amazon Elasticsearch Service) is a fully managed service that makes it easy to deploy, operate, and scale OpenSearch clusters, which are ideal for log analytics, full-text search, and real-time application monitoring. Option A (Amazon RDS) is for relational databases. Option B (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database. Option D (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_45',
  'A company is modernizing its application portfolio. They have a legacy monolithic application running on Amazon EC2 and want to break it down into smaller, independently deployable services using containers. They need a fully managed container orchestration service that allows them to run containers without managing the underlying EC2 instances. Which AWS service should they choose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 Container Service (ECS) with EC2 launch type","Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)","AWS Fargate with Amazon ECS","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Fargate with Amazon ECS) is the correct choice. Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers that works with both Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS. It allows running containers without having to provision, configure, or scale clusters of virtual machines. Option A (Amazon EC2 Container Service (ECS) with EC2 launch type) requires managing the underlying EC2 instances. Option B (Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)) is a managed Kubernetes service, but by itself, it still requires managing worker nodes unless Fargate is used as the compute engine. Option D (AWS Lambda) is for serverless functions, not for containerized microservices that might require longer runtimes or specific container images.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_46',
  'Which AWS service provides highly available and durable object storage for various use cases, including backups, archives, and data lakes?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)","Amazon FSx for Lustre"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)) is the correct answer. Amazon S3 is an object storage service offering industry-leading scalability, data availability, security, and performance. It is ideal for a wide range of use cases including data lakes, websites, mobile applications, backup and restore, archive, and IoT devices. Option A (Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)) provides block storage for Amazon EC2 instances. Option C (Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)) provides scalable file storage for EC2 instances. Option D (Amazon FSx for Lustre) provides high-performance file systems for compute-intensive workloads.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_47',
  'Which AWS service is a fully managed, scalable, and highly available file storage service that can be accessed concurrently by multiple Amazon EC2 instances?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)","Amazon RDS"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)) is the correct answer. EFS provides scalable file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, making it ideal for workloads that require shared file access. Option A (Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)) provides block storage for a single EC2 instance. Option B (Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)) is object storage, not a file system. Option D (Amazon RDS) is a relational database service, not a file storage service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_48',
  'Which AWS service provides managed block storage volumes for use with Amazon EC2 instances?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)","Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)","Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","Amazon FSx for Windows File Server"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)) is the correct answer. EBS provides persistent block storage volumes for use with Amazon EC2 instances, functioning like a raw, unformatted hard drive that can be attached to a single EC2 instance. Option A (Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)) is object storage. Option B (Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)) is a scalable file system. Option D (Amazon FSx for Windows File Server) provides fully managed native Microsoft Windows file systems.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_49',
  'A company needs to run containerized applications and requires a managed Kubernetes service to orchestrate them. They want to leverage the open-source Kubernetes ecosystem while offloading the management of the Kubernetes control plane to AWS. Which service should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 Container Service (ECS)","AWS Fargate","Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)) is the correct choice. EKS is a managed service that makes it easy to run Kubernetes on AWS without needing to install, operate, and maintain your own Kubernetes control plane. Option A (Amazon EC2 Container Service (ECS)) is AWS''s proprietary container orchestration service. Option B (AWS Fargate) is a serverless compute engine for containers that can be used with both ECS and EKS, but it''s not the orchestration service itself. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service for functions, not container orchestration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_3_50',
  'Which AWS service provides fully managed, native Microsoft Windows file systems, accessible via the Server Message Block (SMB) protocol?',
