  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon FSx for Windows File Server) is the correct answer. This service provides a fully managed, highly reliable, and scalable native Microsoft Windows file system that is accessible via the industry-standard Server Message Block (SMB) protocol. Option A (Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)) is for Linux-based workloads. Option B (Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)) is object storage. Option D (Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)) provides block storage for EC2 instances.',
