INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_38',
  'A company wants to decouple microservices in an event-driven architecture. They need a service that can route events from various sources (AWS services, SaaS applications, custom applications) to multiple targets. Which AWS service is best suited for this event routing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is the correct choice. Amazon EventBridge is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services. It allows you to set up rules to filter and route events to various targets. Option A (Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)) is a message queue service for decoupling, but it''s point-to-point or fan-out via SNS. Option B (Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)) is a pub/sub messaging service, primarily for fan-out to multiple subscribers, but EventBridge offers more advanced event routing and filtering capabilities. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows, not primarily for event routing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_39',
  'A company is building a new application that requires a highly scalable, key-value and document database with millisecond latency at any scale. They want a fully managed, serverless solution. Which AWS database service should they choose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon RDS for MySQL","Amazon Aurora","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Redshift"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon DynamoDB) is the correct choice. DynamoDB is a fully managed, serverless NoSQL database service that provides fast and flexible performance with seamless scalability. It''s designed for applications that need consistent, single-digit millisecond latency at any scale. Option A (Amazon RDS for MySQL) and Option B (Amazon Aurora) are relational databases. Option D (Amazon Redshift) is a data warehousing service, not a transactional NoSQL database.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_40',
  'A Solutions Architect is designing an event-driven architecture where multiple downstream services need to be notified when a new order is placed. The solution must support fan-out messaging to various subscribers (e.g., email, SQS queues, Lambda functions). Which AWS service is best suited for this pub/sub pattern?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)) is the correct choice. SNS is a fully managed pub/sub messaging service that enables you to send messages to a large number of subscribers simultaneously. It supports various endpoint types, including email, SQS queues, Lambda functions, and HTTP/S endpoints, making it ideal for fan-out scenarios. Option A (Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)) is a message queue for point-to-point or asynchronous processing, not primarily for fan-out. Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for routing events, but SNS is more direct for simple pub/sub fan-out. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows, not a messaging service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_41',
  'A company needs to process a large backlog of messages asynchronously between different components of its distributed application. They require a fully managed, highly available, and scalable message queuing service. Which AWS service should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)) is the correct choice. SQS is a fully managed message queuing service that enables you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications. It provides a reliable, highly available, and scalable way to send, store, and receive messages between software components. Option A (Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)) is a pub/sub messaging service for fan-out. Option B (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for routing events. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows, not primarily a message queue.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  86,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_42',
  'Which AWS service enables you to run code without provisioning or managing servers, automatically scaling your application in response to demand?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS)","AWS Lambda","Amazon Lightsail"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Lambda) is the correct choice. AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service that lets you run code without provisioning or managing servers. It executes your code only when needed and scales automatically, from a few requests per day to thousands per second. Option A (Amazon EC2) requires provisioning and managing virtual servers. Option B (Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS)) is a container orchestration service that typically runs on EC2 instances or Fargate, which still involves some level of server management or configuration. Option D (Amazon Lightsail) is a simplified cloud platform for small applications, but it still involves virtual servers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  87,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_43',
  'A company needs to modernize a batch processing workload that currently runs on a scheduled cron job on an on-premises server. They want to move this to a serverless architecture, triggered by events, and capable of executing code for up to 15 minutes. Which AWS service is best suited for this?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) on EC2","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Lambda) is the correct choice for serverless execution triggered by events. While Lambda functions have a default timeout of 3 seconds, they can be configured to run for up to 15 minutes, making them suitable for many batch processing tasks. Option A (Amazon EC2) requires server management. Option C (Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) on EC2) involves managing container instances. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows, often using Lambda functions as steps, but Lambda itself is the compute service for the code execution.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  88,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_44',
  'A Solutions Architect needs to orchestrate a series of serverless functions and microservices into a long-running, fault-tolerant workflow. The workflow involves multiple steps, including data processing, human approval, and conditional logic. Which AWS service is designed for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Lambda","Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (AWS Step Functions) is the correct choice. AWS Step Functions is a serverless workflow service that lets you combine AWS Lambda functions and other AWS services to build business-critical applications. You design workflows as state machines, which can handle complex logic, error handling, retries, and human approvals, making them ideal for orchestrating long-running, fault-tolerant processes. Option A (AWS Lambda) executes individual functions. Option B (Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)) is a message queue. Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for routing events.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  89,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_45',
  'A company wants to modernize its application by adopting a microservices architecture using containers. They need to run these containers without managing the underlying servers, ensuring high availability and automatic scaling. Which combination of AWS services provides this serverless container experience?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 with Docker","Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) with EC2 worker nodes","AWS Fargate with Amazon ECS","AWS Lambda with container images"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Fargate with Amazon ECS) is the correct choice. AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers that works with Amazon ECS (and EKS). It allows you to run containers without having to provision, configure, or scale clusters of virtual machines, providing a truly serverless experience for containerized applications. Option A (Amazon EC2 with Docker) requires manual server management. Option B (Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) with EC2 worker nodes) still requires managing the EC2 worker nodes. Option D (AWS Lambda with container images) is for running functions, not full-fledged containerized microservices that might require longer runtimes or specific networking patterns not typical for Lambda.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  90,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_46',
  'Which AWS service enables you to run containerized applications on a fully managed platform without needing to provision or manage servers, offering a serverless operational model for containers?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","AWS Fargate","Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) on EC2"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Fargate) is the correct answer. AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers that works with both Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS. It allows you to run containers without provisioning or managing servers, providing a serverless operational model. Option A (Amazon EC2) requires managing virtual servers. Option B (AWS Lambda) is for serverless functions, not containerized applications in the traditional sense. Option D (Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) on EC2) requires managing the underlying EC2 instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  91,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_47',
  'A company is modernizing its data analytics platform. They need a fully managed, scalable service for real-time processing of streaming data from various sources. Which AWS service is designed for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SQS","Amazon Kinesis","Amazon RDS","Amazon S3"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon Kinesis) is the correct choice. Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service that provides powerful capabilities for processing large streams of data in real time. It can ingest, process, and analyze streaming data to deliver timely insights. Option A (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service for asynchronous communication. Option C (Amazon RDS) is a relational database service. Option D (Amazon S3) is object storage, suitable for storing streaming data after it''s processed, but not for real-time processing itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  92,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_48',
  'A Solutions Architect is tasked with migrating a legacy application that uses a traditional message broker to AWS. The application components need to communicate asynchronously and reliably. The new solution must be fully managed and highly scalable. Which AWS service is best suited for this?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 with RabbitMQ","Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)","Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS)) is the correct choice. SQS is a fully managed message queuing service that enables you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications. It provides a reliable, highly available, and scalable way to send, store, and receive messages asynchronously. Option A (Amazon EC2 with RabbitMQ) would require self-management of the message broker. Option B (Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)) is a pub/sub service, primarily for fan-out, not a message queue for individual component communication. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is for orchestrating workflows, not a messaging service itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  93,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_4_49',
  'A company needs to modernize its application by breaking a monolithic service into smaller, independent components. These components will be deployed as serverless functions that respond to HTTP requests and process data. Which AWS service is ideal for this serverless compute requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2","Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS)","AWS Lambda","Amazon Lightsail"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Lambda) is the correct choice. AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service that allows you to run code without provisioning or managing servers. It''s ideal for creating small, independent functions that can respond to various events, including HTTP requests via Amazon API Gateway, making it perfect for serverless microservices. Option A (Amazon EC2) requires managing virtual servers. Option B (Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS)) is for container orchestration, which can be serverless with Fargate, but Lambda is more granular for individual functions. Option D (Amazon Lightsail) is a simplified cloud platform for small applications, but not a serverless function service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  94,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_4',
  'medium'
);

