  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_43_m_43_5_87',
  'A media company wants to distribute its video content globally with low latency and high transfer speeds. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to configure an Amazon CloudFront distribution for web content delivery.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the video content or configure an existing web server as an origin.","Configure caching behaviors, viewer protocols (HTTP/HTTPS), and geographic restrictions for the distribution.","Create a new Amazon CloudFront web distribution, specifying the origin and default cache behavior.","Update DNS records (e.g., CNAME) to point the domain name to the CloudFront distribution''s domain name."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'The first step in setting up a CloudFront distribution is to define where the content originates. Option A (Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the video content or configure an existing web server as an origin) establishes the source. Next, the CloudFront distribution itself needs to be created and linked to this origin. Option C (Create a new Amazon CloudFront web distribution, specifying the origin and default cache behavior) sets up the CDN. After the distribution is created, its specific behaviors and security settings can be fine-tuned. Option B (Configure caching behaviors, viewer protocols (HTTP/HTTPS), and geographic restrictions for the distribution) allows for optimization and access control. Finally, to direct user traffic through CloudFront, DNS needs to be updated. Option D (Update DNS records (e.g., CNAME) to point the domain name to the CloudFront distribution''s domain name) makes the distribution accessible via the desired domain.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain43_9',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_43_5',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_43_m_43_5_88',
  'A solutions architect needs to implement a caching layer for a high-traffic web application to improve database performance and reduce latency. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to set up an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis cluster.',
  'ordering',
  '["Launch the ElastiCache for Redis cluster, specifying node type, number of shards, and replication groups.","Configure the application to connect to the ElastiCache endpoint for caching operations.","Create a new Amazon VPC Security Group to allow inbound traffic to the ElastiCache cluster from the application''s EC2 instances.","Determine the appropriate Redis engine version, node type, and cluster mode (cluster mode enabled or disabled) based on application requirements."]'::json,
  '{3,2,0,1}',
  'Before launching an ElastiCache cluster, it''s essential to plan its configuration. Option D (Determine the appropriate Redis engine version, node type, and cluster mode (cluster mode enabled or disabled) based on application requirements) defines the technical specifications. Next, network access must be secured. Option C (Create a new Amazon VPC Security Group to allow inbound traffic to the ElastiCache cluster from the application''s EC2 instances) ensures the application can communicate with the cache. Once the network and configuration are ready, the cluster can be provisioned. Option A (Launch the ElastiCache for Redis cluster, specifying node type, number of shards, and replication groups) deploys the caching service. Finally, the application needs to be updated to utilize the new cache. Option B (Configure the application to connect to the ElastiCache endpoint for caching operations) integrates the cache into the application workflow.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain43_9',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_43_5',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_43_m_43_5_89',
  'A database administrator needs to improve the read performance and availability of an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to create and utilize an Amazon RDS Read Replica.',
  'ordering',
  '["Modify the application to direct read queries to the Read Replica endpoint.","Ensure the source RDS DB instance has automatic backups enabled.","Create a Read Replica from the source RDS DB instance, selecting the desired instance type and Multi-AZ option.","Monitor the Read Replica''s performance and replication lag using Amazon CloudWatch."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Before creating a Read Replica, the source database must be configured appropriately. Option B (Ensure the source RDS DB instance has automatic backups enabled) is a prerequisite for creating a Read Replica. Once the source is ready, the Read Replica can be provisioned. Option C (Create a Read Replica from the source RDS DB instance, selecting the desired instance type and Multi-AZ option) deploys the read-only copy. To leverage the Read Replica for performance, the application needs to be updated. Option A (Modify the application to direct read queries to the Read Replica endpoint) offloads read traffic. Finally, it''s crucial to ensure the Read Replica is functioning as expected. Option D (Monitor the Read Replica''s performance and replication lag using Amazon CloudWatch) helps identify any issues and ensures data consistency.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain43_9',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_43_5',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_43_m_43_5_90',
  'A data engineering team needs to upload very large files (e.g., several gigabytes) to Amazon S3 efficiently and reliably. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to perform an S3 multipart upload.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload each part of the file in parallel, specifying the part number.","Initiate a multipart upload request to Amazon S3, receiving an Upload ID.","Combine all uploaded parts into a single object by sending a ''CompleteMultipartUpload'' request with the Upload ID and part ETag information.","Divide the large file into smaller, fixed-size parts (e.g., 5 MB or larger)."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}',
  'The first step in a multipart upload is to prepare the data. Option D (Divide the large file into smaller, fixed-size parts (e.g., 5 MB or larger)) breaks the file into manageable chunks. Next, the multipart upload process needs to be formally started with S3. Option B (Initiate a multipart upload request to Amazon S3, receiving an Upload ID) gets a unique identifier for this specific upload. Once initiated, the individual parts can be uploaded. Option A (Upload each part of the file in parallel, specifying the part number) sends the data segments to S3. Finally, after all parts are uploaded, they need to be assembled into the complete object. Option C (Combine all uploaded parts into a single object by sending a ''CompleteMultipartUpload'' request with the Upload ID and part ETag information) finalizes the upload.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain43_9',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_43_5',
  'medium'
);

