INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_85',
  'A solutions architect is preparing to conduct an AWS Well-Architected Framework review for an existing application. Order the following general steps for conducting such a review.',
  'ordering',
  '["Implement identified improvements and re-evaluate.","Identify areas for improvement based on the pillars.","Define the scope of the workload to be reviewed.","Document current state and gather information."]'::json,
  '{2,3,1,0}',
  'The correct order for conducting an AWS Well-Architected Framework review is to first define the scope, then document the current state, identify areas for improvement, and finally implement and re-evaluate. Option C (Define the scope of the workload to be reviewed) is the initial step to clearly establish what will be assessed. Option D (Document current state and gather information) follows, as understanding the existing architecture is crucial before making recommendations. Option B (Identify areas for improvement based on the pillars) is the core analysis phase, which comes after data collection. Option A (Implement identified improvements and re-evaluate) is the final, iterative step to apply changes and confirm their effectiveness.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_86',
  'An operations team wants to automate a routine patching process for Amazon EC2 instances using AWS Systems Manager Automation. Order the steps to execute an Automation runbook.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the execution status and review outputs.","Select the Automation document and specify parameters.","Define the target EC2 instances for the automation.","Initiate the Automation execution."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'To execute an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook, the logical sequence begins with selecting the appropriate document. Option B (Select the Automation document and specify parameters) is the first step, as it defines the automation''s purpose and configuration. Option C (Define the target EC2 instances for the automation) specifies which resources the automation will act upon. Option D (Initiate the Automation execution) starts the process. Finally, Option A (Monitor the execution status and review outputs) is essential to ensure the automation ran successfully and to troubleshoot any issues.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_87',
  'To establish basic observability for an application running on Amazon EC2, a solutions architect needs to configure Amazon CloudWatch. Order the steps to collect custom metrics and logs.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure CloudWatch Alarms based on the collected metrics.","Install the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances.","Create custom dashboards to visualize metrics and logs.","Define custom metrics and log groups for collection."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'The correct sequence for setting up basic observability with Amazon CloudWatch for custom metrics and logs starts with agent installation. Option B (Install the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances) is necessary to gather data from the instances. Option D (Define custom metrics and log groups for collection) specifies what data the agent should collect and where it should send it. Option A (Configure CloudWatch Alarms based on the collected metrics) allows for proactive notification of issues. Option C (Create custom dashboards to visualize metrics and logs) is typically done last to provide a consolidated view of the collected data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_88',
  'A development team aims to mature their infrastructure deployment process from manual to fully automated using Infrastructure as Code (IaC). Order the typical progression of IaC maturity.',
  'ordering',
  '["Automate deployment with CI/CD pipelines.","Manual resource provisioning.","Define infrastructure using code templates.","Integrate automated testing for IaC."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'The progression of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) maturity typically starts from manual processes and moves towards full automation. Option B (Manual resource provisioning) represents the initial state. Option C (Define infrastructure using code templates) is the first step towards IaC, where infrastructure is described in code. Option A (Automate deployment with CI/CD pipelines) integrates these templates into an automated delivery process. Finally, Option D (Integrate automated testing for IaC) represents a higher maturity level, ensuring the quality and correctness of the IaC itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_89',
  'A company wants to improve its operational runbooks by moving towards automation. Order the steps to transition a manual runbook to an automated AWS Systems Manager Automation document.',
  'ordering',
  '["Test the new Automation document thoroughly.","Identify a repetitive manual operational task.","Convert manual steps into an Automation document.","Deploy the Automation document for production use."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'The process of automating a manual runbook with AWS Systems Manager Automation begins with identifying the task. Option B (Identify a repetitive manual operational task) is the crucial first step to select a candidate for automation. Option C (Convert manual steps into an Automation document) involves translating the existing manual instructions into a machine-executable format. Option A (Test the new Automation document thoroughly) is critical to ensure the automation works as expected and doesn''t introduce new issues. Option D (Deploy the Automation document for production use) is the final step, making the automation available for operational teams.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_90',
  'A solutions architect needs to centralize application logs from Amazon EC2 instances into Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Order the steps to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a CloudWatch Logs log group.","Configure the CloudWatch Agent to send logs to the log group.","Install the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances.","Verify logs are appearing in the CloudWatch console."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To centralize application logs into Amazon CloudWatch Logs, the first step is to prepare the destination. Option A (Create a CloudWatch Logs log group) provides the logical container for the logs. Option C (Install the CloudWatch Agent on the EC2 instances) is necessary to collect logs from the instances. Option B (Configure the CloudWatch Agent to send logs to the log group) tells the agent where to send the collected logs. Finally, Option D (Verify logs are appearing in the CloudWatch console) confirms that the setup is working correctly.',
