  'A development team wants to establish a continuous improvement process for their existing AWS solution by regularly reviewing their architecture against best practices. Order the steps to effectively integrate the AWS Well-Architected Framework into their operational excellence strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Implement identified improvements and monitor their impact.","Conduct a Well-Architected Review using the AWS Well-Architected Tool.","Prioritize high-risk issues and create an action plan for remediation.","Define the scope of the workload to be reviewed within the Well-Architected Tool."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'To effectively integrate the AWS Well-Architected Framework, the first step is to define the scope of the workload (Option D) to ensure the review is focused. Next, conduct the actual Well-Architected Review using the AWS Well-Architected Tool (Option B) to identify areas for improvement. After the review, prioritize the high-risk issues and create a clear action plan (Option C) for addressing them. Finally, implement the identified improvements and continuously monitor their impact (Option A) to ensure operational excellence is maintained and improved over time. Treating the review as a one-time exercise (an anti-pattern) would negate the continuous improvement aspect.',
