VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_1_108',
  'An operations team needs to automate a routine maintenance task, such as stopping and starting Amazon EC2 instances, across multiple accounts using AWS Systems Manager Automation. Order the steps to create and execute a custom Automation runbook for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Execute the Automation document, specifying target instances and parameters.","Create an IAM role with necessary permissions for Systems Manager to perform actions on EC2.","Define the Automation document''s steps, inputs, and outputs in JSON or YAML.","Upload the custom Automation document to Systems Manager Document Store."]'::json,
  '{2,3,1,0}',
  'The process begins by defining the Automation document''s steps, inputs, and outputs (Option C) in a structured format like JSON or YAML, outlining the desired actions. Once defined, the custom Automation document must be uploaded to the Systems Manager Document Store (Option D) to make it available for use. Before execution, an IAM role with the necessary permissions (Option B) must be created and associated with Systems Manager to allow it to perform actions on the target EC2 instances. Finally, the Automation document can be executed (Option A), specifying the target instances and any required parameters.',
