  'A company wants to improve its observability strategy for a critical application running on Amazon EC2 instances by collecting and correlating metrics, logs, and traces. Order the steps to implement a comprehensive observability solution using AWS services.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure AWS X-Ray for distributed tracing across application components.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch agents on EC2 instances to collect custom metrics and logs.","Create Amazon CloudWatch dashboards and alarms based on collected metrics and logs.","Integrate application code with AWS X-Ray SDK to instrument tracing."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To build a comprehensive observability solution, start by setting up Amazon CloudWatch agents (Option B) on EC2 instances to collect system-level metrics and application logs. Concurrently, integrate the application code with the AWS X-Ray SDK (Option D) to enable distributed tracing, which provides insights into request flows. After instrumentation, configure AWS X-Ray (Option A) to process and visualize these traces. Finally, create Amazon CloudWatch dashboards and alarms (Option C) to visualize the correlated metrics, logs, and traces, enabling proactive monitoring and faster issue resolution.',
