  'A company wants to improve its operational excellence by automating incident response using AWS Systems Manager Automation. Order the steps to create an Automation runbook for common incident remediation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the Automation document''s steps for remediation (e.g., restart EC2, collect logs).","Integrate the Automation document with Amazon EventBridge to trigger on specific alarms.","Upload the Automation document to Systems Manager Document Store.","Test the Automation document in a non-production environment."]'::json,
  '{0,2,3,1}',
  'To automate incident response, first define the Automation document''s steps (Option A) for remediation, such as restarting an EC2 instance or collecting diagnostic logs. Next, upload the Automation document (Option C) to Systems Manager Document Store to make it available for execution. Then, test the Automation document (Option D) thoroughly in a non-production environment to ensure it performs the intended actions correctly and safely. Finally, integrate the Automation document with Amazon EventBridge (Option B) to trigger it automatically based on specific Amazon CloudWatch alarms or other events, enabling automated incident response.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
