  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To use AWS Config for compliance monitoring, first enable AWS Config (Option B) to record configuration changes for specified AWS resources. Next, define AWS Config rules (Option A) to evaluate these resource configurations against desired states or best practices. Then, monitor compliance dashboards and receive notifications (Option D) for non-compliant resources, providing visibility into configuration drift. Finally, remediate non-compliant resources (Option C) based on Config findings, either manually or through automated actions, to maintain a consistent and compliant environment.',
