  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Leveraging AWS Compute Optimizer effectively requires sufficient data and a structured approach. Option B (Ensure EC2 instances have sufficient monitoring data (e.g., CloudWatch metrics)) is a prerequisite, as Compute Optimizer relies on historical metrics to generate recommendations. Option C (Access Compute Optimizer console to view findings) is where the recommendations are presented. Option A (Review Compute Optimizer recommendations and implement changes) involves making decisions and applying the suggested right-sizing. Option D (Monitor performance after applying recommendations) is crucial to validate the impact of the changes.',
