  'Migrating to AWS Graviton-based instances involves assessing compatibility, recompiling, testing, and deploying. Option B (Identify application components compatible with ARM architecture) is the initial assessment to understand the scope of work. Option D (Recompile application code for ARM architecture if necessary) is a crucial step for applications not already built for ARM. Option A (Test the application thoroughly on Graviton instances) ensures functionality and performance on the new architecture. Option C (Deploy the application on Graviton-based EC2 instances) is the final step to run the application in production on Graviton.',
