  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'Improving database query performance with indexing is a systematic process. Option B (Analyze slow query logs to identify problematic queries) is the initial diagnostic step to pinpoint where performance is lacking. Option D (Determine columns frequently used in WHERE clauses or JOINs) helps identify the best candidates for indexing within those problematic queries. Option C (Create appropriate indexes on relevant tables) is the implementation step. Option A (Monitor query performance after index creation) is essential to validate the effectiveness of the new indexes and ensure no new issues were introduced.',
