  'Configuring an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm involves selecting the metric, defining its conditions, specifying actions, and then creating it. Option B (Select the metric to monitor (e.g., CPUUtilization)) is the first step, as it determines what the alarm will track. Option C (Specify the threshold and evaluation period for the alarm) sets the conditions under which the alarm will trigger. Option A (Define the alarm action (e.g., send SNS notification)) specifies what happens when the alarm state changes. Option D (Create the CloudWatch Alarm) finalizes the configuration and activates the alarm.',
