  'To optimize database performance using Amazon RDS Performance Insights, the first step is to enable Amazon RDS Performance Insights (Option B) for the target RDS instance. Once enabled, analyze the Performance Insights dashboard (Option C) to get a visual overview of database load and identify potential bottlenecks. Next, identify the top SQL queries, hosts, or users (Option A) that are consuming the most database resources. Finally, implement database tuning strategies (Option D), such as indexing or query optimization, based on the identified bottlenecks. Option A relies on the dashboard analysis. Option C requires Performance Insights to be enabled. Option D is the remediation step after analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
