  'To right-size Amazon EC2 instances using AWS Compute Optimizer, the initial step is to opt-in to AWS Compute Optimizer (Option C) for the AWS account, allowing it to collect and analyze metrics. After a data collection period, review the recommendations provided by AWS Compute Optimizer (Option A) for under-provisioned or over-provisioned instances. Next, implement the recommended EC2 instance type changes (Option B) to adjust resources. Finally, monitor the performance of the resized instances (Option D) to validate that the changes have improved performance or reduced cost without negatively impacting the workload. Option A requires opting in first. Option B depends on the recommendations. Option D is a post-implementation validation.',
