  '["Test the application thoroughly on the Graviton-based instance type.","Identify compatible Graviton-based instance types for the workload.","Create an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) of the existing EC2 instance.","Launch a new Graviton-based EC2 instance from the AMI and install necessary dependencies."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'The first step for a Graviton migration is to create an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) (Option C) of the existing EC2 instance to capture its current state. Next, identify compatible Graviton-based instance types (Option B) that meet the workload''s requirements. Then, launch a new Graviton-based EC2 instance (Option D) from the created AMI and install any necessary Graviton-specific dependencies or optimized libraries. Finally, thoroughly test the application (Option A) on the new Graviton-based instance type to ensure full functionality and performance benefits before a full cutover.',
