  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To right-size EC2 instances using AWS Compute Optimizer, first enable AWS Compute Optimizer (Option B) in the AWS account to begin collecting and analyzing EC2 metrics. Next, review the EC2 instance right-sizing recommendations (Option A) provided by Compute Optimizer, which suggest optimal instance types. Then, apply the recommended instance type changes (Option C) to the identified underutilized or over-provisioned EC2 instances. Finally, monitor the performance and cost impact (Option D) of the right-sized instances to ensure the changes have a positive effect without degrading application performance.',
