  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To tune database performance, first enable Amazon RDS Performance Insights (Option B) for the database instance to collect and visualize performance data. Next, identify high-latency queries and missing indexes (Option A) by analyzing the Performance Insights dashboard, focusing on top SQL and wait events. Then, implement new indexes or optimize existing slow-running SQL queries (Option C) based on the identified bottlenecks. Finally, monitor the database performance metrics (Option D) after applying changes to ensure the optimizations have improved performance and reduced latency.',
