INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_57',
  'A company is developing a disaster recovery plan for its critical application on AWS. Order the general steps involved in creating and testing a disaster recovery strategy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define Recovery Time Objective (RTO) and Recovery Point Objective (RPO).","Implement the chosen DR strategy (e.g., backup and restore, pilot light).","Identify critical applications and data.","Regularly test the disaster recovery plan."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'Developing a disaster recovery plan is a structured process. Option C (Identify critical applications and data) is the foundational step, as it determines what needs protection. Option A (Define Recovery Time Objective (RTO) and Recovery Point Objective (RPO)) establishes the business requirements for recovery, guiding strategy selection. Option B (Implement the chosen DR strategy (e.g., backup and restore, pilot light)) puts the plan into action. Option D (Regularly test the disaster recovery plan) is crucial to ensure the plan remains effective and can be executed successfully when needed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_58',
  'To improve the reliability of a web application, a solutions architect needs to eliminate single points of failure. Order the general steps to identify and address SPOFs.',
  'ordering',
  '["Implement redundancy (e.g., load balancers, multi-AZ deployments).","Identify components that lack redundancy.","Analyze the application architecture for potential SPOFs.","Monitor the application for improved availability."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Eliminating single points of failure (SPOFs) requires a systematic approach. Option C (Analyze the application architecture for potential SPOFs) is the initial diagnostic step to understand where vulnerabilities might exist. Option B (Identify components that lack redundancy) pinpoints the specific SPOFs within the architecture. Option A (Implement redundancy (e.g., load balancers, multi-AZ deployments)) is the remediation step to add fault tolerance. Option D (Monitor the application for improved availability) is essential to verify the effectiveness of the implemented changes and ensure the SPOFs have been successfully addressed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_59',
  'To distribute incoming traffic and improve the reliability of a web application, a solutions architect decides to use an Application Load Balancer. Order the steps to configure an ALB.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a target group and register instances.","Create the Application Load Balancer.","Configure listeners and rules for traffic routing.","Update DNS records to point to the ALB."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Configuring an Application Load Balancer (ALB) involves several sequential steps. Option B (Create the Application Load Balancer) is the first step, establishing the load balancer itself. Option A (Create a target group and register instances) defines where the ALB will send traffic and which instances it will distribute to. Option C (Configure listeners and rules for traffic routing) specifies how the ALB listens for requests and routes them to target groups. Option D (Update DNS records to point to the ALB) is the final step to direct user traffic to the newly configured load balancer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_60',
  'To enhance data durability and support disaster recovery for critical objects, a solutions architect wants to enable cross-Region replication for an Amazon S3 bucket. Order the steps to configure this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a destination S3 bucket in a different AWS Region.","Configure a replication rule on the source S3 bucket.","Enable versioning on both source and destination buckets.","Verify object replication to the destination bucket."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'Configuring cross-Region replication for Amazon S3 requires setting up the destination, enabling versioning, and then defining the replication rule. Option A (Create a destination S3 bucket in a different AWS Region) is necessary to have a target for replicated objects. Option C (Enable versioning on both source and destination buckets) is a prerequisite for S3 replication to function. Option B (Configure a replication rule on the source S3 bucket) specifies what objects to replicate and to which destination. Option D (Verify object replication to the destination bucket) confirms that the setup is working as expected.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_61',
  'A company wants to improve the reliability of its application by automating recovery actions. Order the steps to implement an automated recovery using AWS Systems Manager Automation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define an AWS Systems Manager Automation document for the recovery steps.","Configure an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm to trigger on a reliability issue.","Associate the CloudWatch Alarm with the Systems Manager Automation document.","Test the automated recovery process in a controlled environment."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To implement automated recovery for reliability, first, configure an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm (Option B) to detect a specific reliability issue (e.g., high error rates, instance health check failure). Next, define an AWS Systems Manager Automation document (Option A) that outlines the precise recovery steps to be taken when the alarm triggers. Then, associate the CloudWatch Alarm with the Systems Manager Automation document (Option C) so that the alarm can invoke the runbook. Finally, test the automated recovery process (Option D) in a controlled environment to ensure it functions as expected and resolves the issue reliably. Option A cannot precede the alarm definition as the recovery is in response to an event. Option C links the alarm to the document. Option D is a critical validation step.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_62',
  'Order the steps to use the AWS Well-Architected Tool to review the Reliability Pillar of an existing workload.',
  'ordering',
  '["Identify high-risk issues and create an action plan for remediation.","Launch the AWS Well-Architected Tool and select the target workload.","Answer questions specific to the Reliability Pillar in the tool.","Review the recommendations and best practices provided for reliability."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'To review the Reliability Pillar, begin by launching the AWS Well-Architected Tool and selecting the target workload (Option B). Next, answer questions specific to the Reliability Pillar (Option C) within the tool to assess the workload''s design against best practices. Then, review the recommendations and best practices (Option D) provided by the tool to understand areas for improvement. Finally, identify high-risk issues and create an action plan (Option A) for remediation to enhance the workload''s reliability. Option A is a follow-up action. Option C requires the tool to be launched and workload selected. Option D is a result of answering the questions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_63',
  'A solutions architect wants to improve application resilience by monitoring critical health metrics. Order the steps to configure Amazon CloudWatch for proactive reliability monitoring.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms for critical thresholds.","Define key health metrics and acceptable thresholds for the application.","Set up Amazon SNS topics for alarm notifications.","Configure resources to send metrics to Amazon CloudWatch."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To configure CloudWatch for proactive reliability monitoring, first, define key health metrics and acceptable thresholds (Option B) for the application. Next, configure resources (e.g., EC2 instances, Lambda functions) to send these metrics to Amazon CloudWatch (Option D). Then, create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms (Option A) that trigger when these metrics breach the defined thresholds. Finally, set up Amazon SNS topics (Option C) and link them to the alarms to receive notifications. Option A requires metrics to be collected and thresholds defined. Option C is the final notification step. Option D must follow metric definition.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_64',
  'Order the steps to use AWS Systems Manager Automation to perform a routine health check and restart unhealthy EC2 instances.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define an Automation document with steps for health checking and restarting.","Configure an Amazon CloudWatch Event Rule to trigger the Automation document on a schedule or event.","Specify the target EC2 instances for the Automation document.","Monitor the execution logs and instance status in Systems Manager."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To use Systems Manager Automation for health checks and restarts, first, define an Automation document (Option A) that specifies the steps for performing a health check and conditionally restarting an unhealthy EC2 instance. Next, specify the target EC2 instances (Option C) that this Automation document will operate on. Then, configure an Amazon CloudWatch Event Rule (Option B) to trigger this Automation document on a schedule or in response to a specific event (e.g., an EC2 state change). Finally, monitor the execution logs and instance status (Option D) in Systems Manager to ensure the process is working correctly. Option B requires the document and targets to be defined. Option C must follow document definition. Option D is a post-execution monitoring step.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_65',
  'A solutions architect wants to improve the reliability of a distributed application. Order the steps to use AWS X-Ray to identify potential single points of failure.',
  'ordering',
  '["Instrument the application components with the AWS X-Ray SDK.","Analyze the X-Ray service map for dependencies and potential bottlenecks.","Deploy the instrumented application and generate representative traffic.","Examine individual traces to understand component interactions and error paths."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To identify single points of failure using AWS X-Ray, first, instrument the application components (Option A) with the AWS X-Ray SDK to collect trace data. Next, deploy the instrumented application and generate representative traffic (Option C) to populate the X-Ray service map and traces. Then, analyze the X-Ray service map (Option B) to visualize dependencies, identify choke points, and observe components with high error rates or latency, which could indicate single points of failure. Finally, examine individual traces (Option D) to understand specific component interactions and error paths in detail. Option B requires traces to be generated. Option C must follow instrumentation. Option D is a deeper analysis step after identifying potential issues from the service map.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_66',
  'Order the steps to implement a basic self-healing mechanism for an EC2 instance using Amazon CloudWatch and AWS Systems Manager.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm to monitor EC2 instance health.","Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document to restart the instance.","Associate the CloudWatch Alarm to invoke the Systems Manager Automation document.","Test the self-healing mechanism by manually stopping the EC2 instance."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To implement a basic self-healing mechanism, first, create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document (Option B) that defines the steps to restart an unhealthy EC2 instance. Next, configure an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm (Option A) to monitor the EC2 instance''s health (e.g., status check failures). Then, associate the CloudWatch Alarm (Option C) to invoke the Systems Manager Automation document when the alarm state changes to ALARM. Finally, test the self-healing mechanism (Option D) by manually stopping the EC2 instance to ensure the automation triggers correctly. Option A must precede Option C. Option C links the alarm to the automation. Option D is a validation step.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
