INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_67',
  'A solutions architect wants to ensure the reliability of an application by regularly checking for configuration drift. Order the steps to use AWS Systems Manager State Manager for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a State Manager association to apply the desired configuration.","Create an AWS Systems Manager document specifying the desired state.","Monitor compliance status and identify instances with configuration drift.","Target EC2 instances or other managed nodes for the association."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To use AWS Systems Manager State Manager for configuration drift, first, create an AWS Systems Manager document (Option B) that specifies the desired state or configuration for your instances. Next, target EC2 instances or other managed nodes (Option D) that the State Manager association will apply to. Then, define a State Manager association (Option A) that links the document to the targets and specifies a schedule for applying the configuration. Finally, monitor compliance status (Option C) in Systems Manager to identify instances that have drifted from the desired configuration. Option A requires the document and targets to be defined. Option C is a monitoring step. Option D must follow document creation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_68',
  'Order the steps to use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor application reliability by tracking error rates.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a CloudWatch Alarm based on the error rate metric.","Identify the metric that represents application error rates (e.g., HTTP 5xx errors).","Configure an SNS topic to receive notifications when the alarm triggers.","Analyze historical error rate data to establish a baseline."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To monitor application reliability by tracking error rates with CloudWatch, first, identify the metric that represents application error rates (Option B), such as HTTP 5xx errors from an Application Load Balancer or Lambda function. Next, analyze historical error rate data (Option D) to establish a baseline for normal operation. Then, create a CloudWatch Alarm (Option A) that triggers when the error rate exceeds an acceptable threshold. Finally, configure an SNS topic (Option C) to receive notifications when the alarm triggers, enabling prompt response to reliability issues. Option A requires a metric to be identified. Option C is the final notification step. Option D provides context for setting alarm thresholds.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_69',
  'A solutions architect needs to ensure high durability and availability for an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. Order the steps to configure a multi-AZ deployment for the database.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the Multi-AZ status and performance using Amazon CloudWatch.","Select the ''Multi-AZ deployment'' option during Amazon RDS instance creation or modification.","Ensure proper network connectivity and security group rules allow replication traffic.","Verify automatic failover functionality by simulating an Availability Zone outage."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To configure a multi-AZ deployment for Amazon RDS, the primary step is to select the ''Multi-AZ deployment'' option (Option B) during the instance creation or modification process. After enabling, ensure proper network connectivity and security group rules (Option C) are configured to allow the primary and standby instances to communicate for replication. Once deployed, monitor the Multi-AZ status and performance (Option A) using Amazon CloudWatch to ensure everything is operating correctly. Finally, verify automatic failover functionality (Option D) by simulating an Availability Zone outage to confirm the system''s resilience.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_70',
  'A company wants to improve the reliability of its data storage by implementing cross-Region replication for Amazon S3 buckets. Order the steps to configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR).',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a destination S3 bucket in a different AWS Region.","Enable versioning on both the source and destination S3 buckets.","Configure a replication rule on the source bucket, specifying the destination.","Grant necessary IAM permissions to the S3 bucket for replication."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To set up S3 Cross-Region Replication, first enable versioning on both the source and destination S3 buckets (Option B), as it is a prerequisite for replication. Next, create a destination S3 bucket (Option A) in a different AWS Region where the replicated objects will be stored. Then, grant the necessary IAM permissions (Option D) to the S3 bucket to allow it to perform replication actions. Finally, configure a replication rule (Option C) on the source bucket, specifying the destination bucket and any filters for objects to be replicated.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_71',
  'A solutions architect needs to implement a robust disaster recovery strategy for an application running on Amazon EC2 instances using AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS). Order the steps to set up DRS for a workload.',
  'ordering',
  '["Install the Elastic Disaster Recovery Agent on the source EC2 instances.","Launch recovery instances in the target AWS Region from the replicated data.","Configure replication settings and target AWS Region in the Elastic Disaster Recovery console.","Monitor data replication progress and perform non-disruptive drill tests."]'::json,
  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'To set up AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS), first configure the replication settings and target AWS Region (Option C) within the DRS console, defining where the recovery will occur. Next, install the Elastic Disaster Recovery Agent (Option A) on the source EC2 instances to begin continuous data replication. Once replication is active, monitor the data replication progress and perform non-disruptive drill tests (Option D) to validate the recovery process without impacting production. Finally, in the event of a disaster, launch recovery instances (Option B) in the target AWS Region from the replicated data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_72',
  'A company wants to improve the reliability of its application by implementing automated self-healing for Amazon EC2 instances that become unhealthy. Order the steps to configure an Auto Scaling group with health checks.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure an Auto Scaling group to use the launch template and desired capacity.","Define a launch template specifying the EC2 instance configuration and AMI.","Set up health checks (e.g., EC2 status checks, ELB health checks) for the Auto Scaling group.","Monitor the Auto Scaling group''s activity and instance health using Amazon CloudWatch."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To implement automated self-healing, first define a launch template (Option B) specifying the EC2 instance configuration, including the AMI, instance type, and user data. Next, configure an Auto Scaling group (Option A) to use this launch template, setting the desired capacity and scaling policies. Then, set up health checks (Option C), such as EC2 status checks or Elastic Load Balancing health checks, for the Auto Scaling group to detect unhealthy instances. Finally, monitor the Auto Scaling group''s activity and instance health (Option D) using Amazon CloudWatch to ensure instances are being replaced automatically when unhealthy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_73',
  'A solutions architect needs to improve the reliability of an application by ensuring its components are deployed across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) to prevent single points of failure. Order the steps to distribute an application across multiple AZs.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) to distribute traffic across instances in different AZs.","Create subnets in different Availability Zones within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).","Deploy application instances into the subnets across multiple AZs.","Set up an Auto Scaling group to maintain desired capacity across AZs."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To distribute an application across multiple AZs, first create subnets in different Availability Zones (Option B) within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) to provide the network foundation. Next, deploy application instances (Option C) into these subnets across the chosen AZs. Then, configure an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) (Option A) to distribute incoming traffic evenly across the instances in different AZs, ensuring high availability. Finally, set up an Auto Scaling group (Option D) to automatically maintain the desired capacity and replace unhealthy instances across these AZs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_74',
  'A solutions architect needs to improve the reliability of an application by implementing a multi-Region disaster recovery strategy. Order the steps to set up active-passive disaster recovery for a web application.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure data replication (e.g., RDS cross-Region replication, S3 Cross-Region Replication) to the DR Region.","Deploy a scaled-down version of the application infrastructure in a secondary (DR) AWS Region.","Set up Amazon Route 53 health checks and failover routing policies.","Perform regular disaster recovery drills to validate the failover process."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To implement active-passive multi-Region disaster recovery, first deploy a scaled-down version of the application infrastructure (Option B) in a secondary (DR) AWS Region, including compute, database, and networking components. Next, configure data replication (Option A) for critical data stores, such as Amazon RDS cross-Region replication or Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication, to ensure data consistency in the DR Region. Then, set up Amazon Route 53 health checks and failover routing policies (Option C) to automatically redirect traffic to the DR Region in case of a primary Region outage. Finally, perform regular disaster recovery drills (Option D) to validate the failover process and ensure readiness.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_75',
  'A solutions architect needs to improve the reliability of a database by ensuring point-in-time recovery and automated backups for an Amazon RDS instance. Order the steps to configure automated backups and restore capabilities.',
  'ordering',
  '["Set the backup retention period for automated backups.","Enable automated backups during Amazon RDS instance creation or modification.","Test point-in-time recovery by restoring the database to a specific timestamp.","Monitor backup status and retention using the RDS console or CloudWatch."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To configure automated backups for Amazon RDS, first enable automated backups (Option B) during instance creation or modification. Next, set the backup retention period (Option A) to define how long the automated backups will be kept. Then, monitor backup status and retention (Option D) using the RDS console or Amazon CloudWatch to ensure backups are occurring successfully. Finally, test point-in-time recovery (Option C) by restoring the database to a specific timestamp to validate the recovery process and ensure data integrity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_44_m_44_4_76',
  'A solutions architect needs to improve the reliability of an application by ensuring its database can recover quickly from failures. Order the steps to configure Amazon Aurora Global Database for multi-Region disaster recovery.',
  'ordering',
  '["Promote a secondary Region cluster to be the new primary in a disaster scenario.","Create an Amazon Aurora database cluster in a primary AWS Region.","Add a secondary Aurora cluster in a different AWS Region to the global database.","Monitor replication lag and health of the global database."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'To configure Amazon Aurora Global Database, first create an Amazon Aurora database cluster (Option B) in a primary AWS Region. Next, add a secondary Aurora cluster (Option C) in a different AWS Region to the global database, establishing cross-Region replication. Then, monitor replication lag and health (Option D) of the global database using Amazon CloudWatch to ensure data consistency and readiness. Finally, in a disaster scenario, promote a secondary Region cluster (Option A) to be the new primary, enabling rapid recovery with minimal data loss.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_44_4',
  'medium'
);

