  'To centralize security findings and gain a comprehensive view of security posture, a solutions architect decides to enable AWS Security Hub. Order the initial steps to set up Security Hub.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable Security Hub in the AWS console.","Integrate other AWS security services (e.g., GuardDuty, Config).","Review security findings and prioritize remediation.","Configure standards (e.g., AWS Foundational Security Best Practices)."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'Setting up AWS Security Hub starts with enabling the service. Option A (Enable Security Hub in the AWS console) is the foundational step. Option D (Configure standards (e.g., AWS Foundational Security Best Practices)) involves selecting the security benchmarks against which your resources will be evaluated. Option B (Integrate other AWS security services (e.g., GuardDuty, Config)) allows Security Hub to ingest findings from various sources. Option C (Review security findings and prioritize remediation) is the ongoing operational step to address identified issues.',
