  'A company is migrating from legacy on-premises security patterns to AWS-native security controls. Order the general steps for this transition.',
  'ordering',
  '["Implement AWS-native security services (e.g., Security Groups, WAF).","Assess current on-premises security controls and identify gaps.","Define security requirements and compliance needs for AWS.","Decommission legacy security infrastructure."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Migrating to AWS-native security controls is a strategic process. Option B (Assess current on-premises security controls and identify gaps) is the initial discovery phase to understand the existing security posture. Option C (Define security requirements and compliance needs for AWS) translates business and regulatory needs into cloud-specific security objectives. Option A (Implement AWS-native security services (e.g., Security Groups, WAF)) is the execution phase, deploying the new controls. Option D (Decommission legacy security infrastructure) is the final step, removing old systems once the new ones are fully operational and validated.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain44_9',
