  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To configure Amazon GuardDuty for threat detection, the first step is to enable Amazon GuardDuty (Option B) in the AWS account. Next, configure trusted IP lists and threat lists (Option C) to refine GuardDuty''s detection capabilities and reduce false positives. Then, review GuardDuty findings (Option A) and investigate any suspicious activities reported. Finally, set up Amazon EventBridge rules (Option D) to send GuardDuty findings to a central security system or for automated remediation. Option A requires GuardDuty to be enabled and generating findings. Option C helps refine detection. Option D is for automated processing of findings.',
