  'To use AWS IAM Access Analyzer, first, enable IAM Access Analyzer (Option B) for the AWS account to begin scanning resource policies. Next, review the findings generated by IAM Access Analyzer (Option A), which highlight resources accessible from outside the account. Then, remediate external access (Option D) by modifying the identified resource policies to restrict unintended access. Finally, generate a least-privilege policy (Option C) based on Access Analyzer findings to ensure future policies adhere to security best practices. Option A requires Access Analyzer to be enabled. Option C is a follow-up action after remediation. Option D depends on the findings.',
