  'To migrate to AWS-native network security controls, first, analyze existing network security rules and traffic flows (Option B) to understand current requirements. Next, implement AWS Network Firewall or Security Groups (Option A) to provide granular traffic control within the VPC. Then, transition traffic from legacy firewalls (Option C) to these newly implemented AWS-native controls. Finally, decommission legacy security appliances (Option D) once all traffic has been successfully migrated and validated. Option A requires an understanding of existing rules. Option C depends on the new controls being in place. Option D is the final cleanup step.',
