  'To optimize RDS costs with AWS Compute Optimizer, the initial step is to opt-in to AWS Compute Optimizer (Option B) for the AWS account. After a data collection period, review the Compute Optimizer dashboard (Option A) for RDS instance recommendations, which suggest optimal instance types. Next, implement the recommended RDS instance type changes (Option C) to right-size the database. Finally, monitor the performance and cost (Option D) of the resized RDS instances to validate the optimization and ensure database performance is not negatively impacted. Option A requires Compute Optimizer to be enabled. Option C depends on the recommendations. Option D is a post-implementation validation.',
