  'To use the AWS Well-Architected Tool for cost anti-patterns, first, launch the AWS Well-Architected Tool and define the workload (Option A). Next, answer questions across the Cost Optimization Pillar (Option C) to assess the workload''s design against best practices. Then, review the generated report (Option B) for specific cost optimization anti-patterns and associated risks. Finally, develop and implement an action plan (Option D) to resolve the identified anti-patterns and improve cost efficiency. Option B requires answering the questions. Option C must follow workload definition. Option D is the remediation step.',
