  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To effectively use AWS Compute Optimizer for cost optimization, first enable AWS Compute Optimizer (Option B) in the AWS account to allow it to collect and analyze resource utilization data. Once enabled, analyze the recommendations (Option A) provided by Compute Optimizer for EC2 instances, EBS volumes, Lambda functions, and RDS databases. Next, implement the right-sizing recommendations (Option C) for the identified underutilized resources. Finally, monitor resource utilization and cost savings (Option D) after implementing the changes to validate the optimization and ensure performance is not negatively impacted.',
