INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_53',
  'Which two AWS services assist in discovering on-premises server inventory and tracking migration progress for a large-scale migration project? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Migration Hub","AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS DMS","AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)","AWS Control Tower"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Migration Hub) provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions. Option B (AWS Application Discovery Service) helps you identify servers, databases, and other assets in your on-premises data centers, collecting configuration and performance data for migration planning. Option C (AWS DMS) is for database migration. Option D (AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)) is for server rehosting. Option E (AWS Control Tower) is for multi-account governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_54',
  'When evaluating migration strategies using the 7 Rs, which two approaches involve moving applications to AWS with minimal or no changes to the application architecture? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Refactor","Replatform","Retire","Repurchase"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Rehost), also known as ''lift-and-shift,'' involves moving applications to AWS without making any changes to the application architecture. Option C (Replatform), also known as ''lift-tinker-and-shift,'' involves making a few cloud-native optimizations to realize some benefits without changing the core architecture. Option B (Refactor) involves significant architectural changes to leverage cloud-native features. Option D (Retire) means decommissioning applications. Option E (Repurchase) means moving to a different product, typically SaaS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_55',
  'Which two activities are essential for developing a business case for cloud migration, focusing on financial aspects? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Refactoring applications","Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) analysis","Workload discovery using AWS Application Discovery Service","Identifying cloud-native benefits","Developing a detailed migration plan"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) analysis) is crucial for a business case, as it compares the costs of running IT infrastructure on-premises versus in the cloud over a period. Option D (Identifying cloud-native benefits) helps quantify the value proposition beyond just cost savings, such as increased agility, scalability, and innovation, which are key to a strong business case. Option A (Refactoring applications) is a migration strategy, not directly part of business case development. Option C (Workload discovery using AWS Application Discovery Service) is for inventory, which feeds into TCO but isn''t the analysis itself. Option E (Developing a detailed migration plan) comes after the business case is approved.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_56',
  'Which two AWS services are specifically designed to aid in the discovery of on-premises resources and tracking the migration process to AWS? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS DataSync","AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS Migration Hub","AWS DMS","AWS Control Tower"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (AWS Application Discovery Service) helps you identify servers, databases, and other assets in your on-premises data centers, collecting configuration and performance data. Option C (AWS Migration Hub) provides a single location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions. Option A (AWS DataSync) is for online data transfer. Option D (AWS DMS) is for database migration. Option E (AWS Control Tower) is for multi-account governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_57',
  'When planning a migration, which two of the 7 Rs of migration involve changing how an application is run or consumed, rather than just moving it? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Refactor","Retire","Repurchase","Relocate"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Refactor/Re-architect) involves fundamentally changing the application''s architecture to fully leverage cloud-native capabilities and improve agility, scalability, and performance. Option D (Repurchase) involves moving to a different product, typically a SaaS offering, which changes how the application is consumed. Option A (Rehost) is a lift-and-shift with minimal changes. Option C (Retire) means decommissioning. Option E (Relocate) involves moving hypervisors to EC2 without changing the application, similar to rehost.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_58',
  'A company is performing a portfolio assessment to identify migration candidates. Which two outcomes are common goals of this assessment phase? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Developing new application features","Identifying applications suitable for cloud migration","Determining the optimal migration strategy (e.g., Rehost, Refactor)","Implementing a new CI/CD pipeline","Setting up AWS accounts for the entire organization"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (Identifying applications suitable for cloud migration) is a primary goal of a portfolio assessment, categorizing which applications are good candidates. Option C (Determining the optimal migration strategy (e.g., Rehost, Refactor)) for each identified application is also a key outcome, aligning the application with one of the 7 Rs. Option A (Developing new application features) is a post-migration activity. Option D (Implementing a new CI/CD pipeline) is part of modernization, often after migration. Option E (Setting up AWS accounts for the entire organization) is part of foundational setup, often preceding detailed migration planning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_59',
  'Which two of the 7 Rs of migration involve eliminating or replacing existing applications or systems? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Retire","Replatform","Repurchase","Refactor"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (Retire) involves decommissioning applications that are no longer needed, eliminating them from the portfolio. Option D (Repurchase) involves replacing an existing application with a new, typically SaaS-based, product, effectively eliminating the old system. Option A (Rehost), Option C (Replatform), and Option E (Refactor) all involve migrating and continuing to use the application, albeit with different levels of modification.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_60',
  'A company is evaluating its on-premises data centers for potential migration to AWS. They need to identify all servers, applications, and network dependencies to build a comprehensive migration plan. Which AWS services can assist with discovering and mapping their on-premises environment? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS Migration Hub","AWS DataSync","AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT)","AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Application Discovery Service) is specifically designed to help plan migration projects by identifying on-premises applications, their dependencies, and performance profiles. Option B (AWS Migration Hub) provides a single location to track the progress of migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions, and it integrates with AWS Application Discovery Service for discovery data. Option C (AWS DataSync) is for online data transfer, not discovery. Option D (AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT)) is for database schema conversion. Option E (AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)) is for rehosting servers, not for initial discovery.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_61',
  'When evaluating existing workloads for migration to AWS, a Solutions Architect needs to categorize them based on the ''7 Rs of Migration'' strategy. Which of the following are valid ''R'' strategies? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Refactor","Replicate","Relocate","Re-evaluate"]'::json,
  '{0,1,3}',
  'Option A (Rehost), Option B (Refactor), and Option D (Relocate) are all valid strategies within the ''7 Rs of Migration'' framework. Rehost (lift-and-shift) moves applications without changes. Refactor (re-architect) reimagines how an application is architected and developed. Relocate moves hypervisors or entire environments without purchasing new hardware, re-writing applications, or modifying existing operations. Option C (Replicate) is not one of the standard 7 Rs. Option E (Re-evaluate) is a step in the process but not one of the 7 R strategies.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_62',
  'A company has several legacy applications running on aging on-premises servers. They want to move these applications to AWS with the LEAST amount of application code change, while still leveraging cloud benefits. Which migration strategies are most suitable for these applications? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Refactor","Replatform","Retire","Repurchase"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Rehost), also known as ''lift-and-shift,'' involves moving applications to AWS without making any changes to the application architecture, minimizing code changes. Option C (Replatform) involves making some cloud-native optimizations to the application to achieve tangible benefits without changing the core architecture, such as migrating to a managed database service. Option B (Refactor) involves significant code changes to fully leverage cloud-native capabilities, which contradicts the ''least amount of code change'' requirement. Option D (Retire) means decommissioning applications, which is not a migration. Option E (Repurchase) involves moving to a different product, typically SaaS, which would involve significant changes from the existing application.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  79,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_63',
  'Which of the following are valid ''R'' strategies within the AWS 7 Rs of Migration framework? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Rehost","Retire","Rebuild","Replatform","Redesign"]'::json,
  '{0,1,3}',
  'Option A (Rehost), Option B (Retire), and Option D (Replatform) are all recognized strategies within the AWS 7 Rs of Migration framework. Rehost involves moving applications without changes. Retire means decommissioning applications that are no longer needed. Replatform involves making some cloud-native optimizations without changing the core architecture. Option C (Rebuild) and Option E (Redesign) are not standard terms in the 7 Rs, though ''Refactor'' (which is similar to redesign/rebuild) is. The 7 Rs are: Rehost, Replatform, Refactor, Repurchase, Retain, Retire, Relocate.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  80,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_64',
  'A Solutions Architect is performing a migration readiness assessment for an on-premises environment. Which of the following are key benefits of using AWS Application Discovery Service? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Collects server configuration and performance data","Automates database schema conversion","Maps application dependencies","Performs server rehosting to EC2","Provides a central dashboard for migration tracking"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Collects server configuration and performance data) is a primary function of AWS Application Discovery Service, gathering details like CPU, memory, disk usage, and network information. Option C (Maps application dependencies) is another key benefit, as it helps visualize connections between applications, servers, and databases, which is crucial for migration planning. Option B (Automates database schema conversion) is handled by AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT). Option D (Performs server rehosting to EC2) is the function of AWS Application Migration Service (MGN). Option E (Provides a central dashboard for migration tracking) is the role of AWS Migration Hub.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  81,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_65',
  'A company is planning to migrate a portfolio of applications to AWS. They want to use AWS Migration Hub to centralize the tracking of their migration progress. Which of the following capabilities does AWS Migration Hub provide? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Provides a single dashboard for tracking migrations","Automates the rehosting of servers to EC2","Integrates with various AWS migration tools","Performs real-time database replication","Discovers on-premises server inventory"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Provides a single dashboard for tracking migrations) is a core feature of AWS Migration Hub, offering a unified view of migration progress across different tools and applications. Option C (Integrates with various AWS migration tools) is also a key capability, allowing Migration Hub to pull data from services like AWS Application Migration Service (MGN), AWS Database Migration Service (DMS), and partner solutions. Option B (Automates the rehosting of servers to EC2) is handled by AWS Application Migration Service (MGN). Option D (Performs real-time database replication) is a function of AWS Database Migration Service (DMS). Option E (Discovers on-premises server inventory) is primarily handled by AWS Application Discovery Service, which can then feed data into Migration Hub.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_66',
  'A Solutions Architect is advising a client on migration strategies for their diverse application portfolio. The client wants to minimize operational effort and realize cloud-native benefits where appropriate. Which of the following strategies align with this goal? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Refactor","Repurchase","Rehost all applications to minimize initial effort","Retain all applications on-premises","Relocate virtual machines to VMware Cloud on AWS"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Refactor) involves re-architecting applications to fully leverage cloud-native capabilities, which significantly minimizes operational effort in the long run and maximizes cloud benefits. Option B (Repurchase) involves moving to a SaaS solution, which completely offloads operational overhead to the SaaS provider. Option C (Rehost all applications to minimize initial effort) is an anti-pattern ([ap-4.1-001]) because while it minimizes initial effort, it moves technical debt to the cloud without realizing significant cloud-native benefits or operational efficiency gains. Option D (Retain all applications on-premises) does not involve migration or realizing cloud benefits. Option E (Relocate virtual machines to VMware Cloud on AWS) is a specific type of rehost/relocate that maintains a VMware environment, which might not fully minimize operational effort or realize cloud-native benefits compared to refactoring or repurchasing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_67',
  'A company is migrating its on-premises applications to AWS. They need to identify all running processes, network connections, and resource utilization of their servers to understand their current state and plan for right-sizing in the cloud. Which AWS services can provide this detailed operational data? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Application Discovery Service","AWS Migration Hub","AWS DataSync","AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT)","AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Application Discovery Service) collects detailed configuration and performance data from on-premises servers, including running processes, network connections, and resource utilization, which is essential for right-sizing and migration planning. Option B (AWS Migration Hub) serves as a central hub that aggregates discovery data from AWS Application Discovery Service and other tools, providing a consolidated view of the on-premises environment and tracking migration progress. Option C (AWS DataSync) is for data transfer, not discovery. Option D (AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT)) is for database schema conversion. Option E (AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)) is for rehosting servers, not for initial discovery and data collection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  84,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_68',
  'A large enterprise is planning to migrate a critical, monolithic on-premises application with significant technical debt to AWS. The application is business-critical, but its current architecture hinders innovation and scalability. The leadership team wants to embrace cloud-native patterns and improve developer agility, rather than simply rehosting. Which two migration strategies should the solutions architect prioritize to achieve these long-term goals? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Option A: Rehost the application using AWS Application Migration Service (MGN) to quickly move it to Amazon EC2, then optimize later.","Option B: Refactor the application by breaking it into microservices and deploying them on AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS.","Option C: Replatform the application by migrating its components to managed AWS services like Amazon RDS and Amazon ECS Fargate.","Option D: Repurchase a SaaS solution that provides similar functionality to replace the existing application entirely.","Option E: Retain the application on-premises due to the high effort involved in refactoring."]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (correct) involves refactoring, which means re-architecting the application to take full advantage of cloud-native capabilities, such as microservices on AWS Lambda and Amazon ECS. This directly addresses the goal of embracing cloud-native patterns and improving agility. Option C (correct) suggests replatforming, which involves moving to managed AWS services (like Amazon RDS for databases and Amazon ECS Fargate for containers) to reduce operational overhead and gain cloud benefits without a full re-architecture. Both refactoring and replatforming are suitable for achieving long-term cloud-native benefits and agility. Option A (incorrect) describes rehosting, which is a lift-and-shift approach. While it offers a quick migration, it moves technical debt to the cloud without realizing significant cloud-native benefits, which contradicts the stated goal of embracing cloud-native patterns. This aligns with anti-pattern ap-4.1-001. Option D (incorrect) is repurchase, which might be a valid strategy for some workloads but is not a direct migration strategy for an existing application that the company wants to modernize and operate. Option E (incorrect) suggests retaining the application on-premises, which goes against the objective of migrating to AWS and improving the application''s architecture.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  85,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_45_1',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_69',
  'A global manufacturing company operates hundreds of on-premises servers and virtual machines across various data centers. They need to gain a comprehensive understanding of their server inventory, network dependencies, and application performance profiles to inform their cloud migration strategy. The goal is to automate data collection and centralize visibility into their entire IT estate. Which two AWS services should a Solutions Architect recommend for automated discovery and centralized migration tracking? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Option A: AWS Migration Hub to provide a single dashboard for tracking migration progress across multiple tools.","Option B: AWS Application Discovery Service to automatically collect configuration, performance, and dependency data from on-premises servers.","Option C: AWS Config to monitor and record AWS resource configurations and changes over time.","Option D: AWS Systems Manager to manage and automate operational tasks across EC2 instances and on-premises servers.","Option E: Amazon CloudWatch to collect and track metrics, collect log files, and set alarms for AWS resources."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Migration Hub, which provides a central location to track the progress of application migrations across multiple AWS and partner solutions. This directly addresses the need for centralized visibility and tracking. Option B (correct) is AWS Application Discovery Service, which helps plan migration projects by automatically identifying applications running in on-premises data centers, their associated dependencies, and performance profiles. This service is crucial for automated data collection and understanding the IT estate. Option C (incorrect) is AWS Config, which is primarily used for monitoring and recording configurations of AWS resources, not for discovering on-premises assets for migration planning. Option D (incorrect) is AWS Systems Manager, which is used for operational management and automation of instances, but not its primary purpose is not on-premises discovery for migration planning. Option E (incorrect) is Amazon CloudWatch, which is a monitoring service for AWS resources and applications, not for on-premises discovery or centralized migration tracking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain45_9',
  NOW(),
  86,
  NULL,
  NULL,
