VALUES (
  'q_45_m_45_1_97',
  'An organization is performing a Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) analysis to justify migrating its on-premises workloads to AWS. Order the following steps for conducting a TCO analysis.',
  'ordering',
  '["Estimate the costs of running the workloads on AWS, including compute, storage, and networking.","Identify and quantify all current on-premises costs, such as hardware, software licenses, power, and administration.","Compare the on-premises costs with the estimated AWS costs over a defined period.","Present the TCO analysis findings to stakeholders for decision-making."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'A TCO analysis starts by understanding the current state, which involves identifying and quantifying all existing on-premises costs (Option B). Then, the estimated costs of running the workloads on AWS are calculated (Option A). These two sets of costs are then compared (Option C) to determine the financial benefits or implications of migration. Finally, the findings are presented to stakeholders (Option D) to inform strategic decisions.',
