  'Improving resilience starts by identifying single points of failure (Option A) in the current architecture. Next, redundancy (Option B) is implemented by distributing components across multiple Availability Zones. Then, the architecture is designed for fault isolation (Option C) to contain failures. Finally, regular testing of failure scenarios (Option D) ensures the resilience measures are effective.',
