  '["Verify `kubectl` context is set to the EKS cluster","Install `kubectl` and AWS CLI","Update `kubeconfig` using AWS CLI `update-kubeconfig` command","Retrieve the EKS cluster name and Region"]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'To configure `kubectl` for EKS, first install `kubectl` and AWS CLI (Option B) on your local machine. Next, retrieve the EKS cluster name and Region (Option D) from the AWS console or CLI. Then, update your `kubeconfig` file using the AWS CLI `update-kubeconfig` command (Option C), which adds the cluster''s context. Finally, verify that the `kubectl` context is set to the EKS cluster (Option A) to ensure successful communication.',
