  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'The initial steps for migrating an on-premises Kubernetes deployment to EKS begin by setting up a dedicated VPC and subnets (Option C) that meet EKS networking requirements. Next, provision an Amazon EKS cluster and its associated node groups (Option A). Then, configure `kubectl` and AWS CLI (Option D) to establish access to the newly created EKS cluster. Finally, analyze the existing Kubernetes manifests (Option B) to identify any necessary adjustments for AWS compatibility.',
